resident Who Doesn’t Go by the (History) Book', 'kicker': 'White House Memo', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'This President Doesn’t Go by the (History) Book', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidents and Presidency (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Andrew', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-02T07:30:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker and Jonah Engel Bromwich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jonah', 'middlename': 'Engel', 'lastname': 'Bromwich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f9eede5-e857-57e5-bb40-2dd49536ca94', 'word_count': 1399, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f9eede5-e857-57e5-bb40-2dd49536ca94'}, {'abstract': 'Four decades ago, Jamel Shabazz set out to photograph black and Latino young people in New York City and explore the uplifting power of style, fashion, music and culture.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2017/05/02/jamel-shabazzs-40-years-of-sights-and-styles-in-new-york/', 'snippet': 'Four decades ago, Jamel Shabazz set out to photograph black and Latino young people in New York City and explore the uplifting power of style, fashion, music and culture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Jamel Shabazz began photographing New York in 1980, the city was recovering from one of its most tumultuous periods. By the late-1970s, New York was facing a faltering economy, a serious drug problem and the physical deterioration of many neighborhoods. New York was ripe for sociological analysis and hand-wringing. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jamel Shabazz’s 40 Years of Sights and Styles in New York', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shabazz, Jamel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-02T08:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maurice Berger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maurice', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62301a51-6719-50eb-8ee6-b2a13c1a565c', 'word_count': 1012, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62301a51-6719-50eb-8ee6-b2a13c1a565c'}, {'abstract': 'How did two Slovakian high schoolers start a movement against political corruption?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/02/learning/questions-for-young-idealistic-but-determined-slovaks-lead-anticorruption-crusade.html', 'snippet': 'How did two Slovakian high schoolers start a movement against political corruption?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Article: Young, Idealistic but Determined, Slovaks Lead Anticorruption Crusade', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/23/world/00corruption1/00corruption1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/04/23/world/00corruption1/00corruption1-ar