rganization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/090d3a84-fb81-5a8e-af80-50bd8bc13ef9', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/090d3a84-fb81-5a8e-af80-50bd8bc13ef9'}, {'abstract': 'Dan Kluger’s new restaurant in Greenwich Village leans heavily on grains and seasonal produce, evoking his work at ABC Kitchen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/02/dining/loring-place-review-greenwich-village.html', 'snippet': 'Dan Kluger’s new restaurant in Greenwich Village leans heavily on grains and seasonal produce, evoking his work at ABC Kitchen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ABC Kitchen signified a small turning point in the appetites of New Yorkers when it opened seven years ago. We had snuffled through much of the previous decade in search of pork shoulders, lamb belly, rib-eyes and marrow bones, and if we didn’t exactly wake up on the first day of 2010 doubled over with regret, some of us were starting to wonder why the bed smelled like bacon.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Vegetable Forward’ Chef Gets His Own Patch at Loring Place', 'kicker': 'Restaurant Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Vegetable Patch of His Own', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kluger, Dan (Chef)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Loring Place (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenwich Village (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-02T16:13:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Wells', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wells', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/02d048be-b11d-56df-9844-e78531390f20', 'word_count': 1132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02d048be-b11d-56df-9844-e78531390f20'}, {'abstract': 'Like the president, many of us believe we could have changed history.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/02/opinion/trump-andrew-jackson-and-ourselves.html', 'snippet': 'Like the president, many of us believe we could have changed history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Trump believes in the “great man” theory of history. Specifically, he believes that a great man, a man like President Andrew Jackson, could have stopped the American Civil War. In an interview with Salena Zito, a reporter for The Washington Examiner, on Sirius XM’s “Main Street Meets the Beltway,” Mr. Trump said the following: “Had Andrew Jackson been a little later you wouldn’t have had the Civil War. He was a very tough person, but he had a big heart, and he was really angry that he saw what was happening with regard to the Civil War. He said, ‘There’s no reason for this.’ ”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/02/opinion/02coastonWeb/02groteWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 834, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/02/opinion/02coastonWeb/02groteWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 834}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/02/opinion/02coastonWeb/02groteWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/02/opinion/02coastonWeb/02groteWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1474, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': Non