: 'Refugees from around the world spend their first night in the U.S. at an airport hotel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The United States has a long, complicated history of accepting refugees from around the world. However, few of us are familiar with the intricacies of how relocation and resettlement works. Back in 2006, after reading an article about an airport hotel that shelters refugees awaiting their connections to far-flung corners of this country, we found ourselves wondering about their very first night here. How did these newcomers navigate that foreign, if quintessentially American environment?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'First Night in America', 'kicker': 'Op-Docs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRPORTS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Organization for Migration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newark (NJ)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Newark Liberty International Airport (NJ)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-02T19:45:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrea Meller and Marisa Pearl', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Meller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Marisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pearl', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c172b983-3ad3-5a93-9416-361385ae6fe0', 'word_count': 492, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c172b983-3ad3-5a93-9416-361385ae6fe0'}, {'abstract': 'Myth, transformation and androgyny: Mr. Williams’s new dance, “Il Giardino d’Amore,” illustrates the affair between Venus and Adonis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/02/arts/dance/christopher-williamss-garden-of-fantastical-delights.html', 'snippet': 'Myth, transformation and androgyny: Mr. Williams’s new dance, “Il Giardino d’Amore,” illustrates the affair between Venus and Adonis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The choreographer Christopher Williams’s works are a bit like a cabinet of curiosities. They reflect his fascination with very old stories, particularly ones that include mythological beings and magical transformations. He has made phantasmagorical dances inspired by the lives — and violent deaths — of the early saints, by Greek mythology and by Scottish fairy tales, among other wild tales. To say he is an artist of peculiar obsessions is an understatement.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/03/arts/03WILLIAMS1/03WILLIAMS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 341, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/03/arts/03WILLIAMS1/03WILLIAMS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 341}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/03/arts/03WILLIAMS1/03WILLIAMS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 582, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/03/arts/03WILLIAMS1/03WILLIAMS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1164, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/03/arts/