of the end of retail as we know it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'About three years ago, like millions of other Instagram users, I became acquainted with an app called Wish. At first, my awareness was purely subliminal. Wish ads appeared in my social-media feeds without explanation or context, peddling a deliriously weird selection of heavily discounted products: a smartwatch for under $20; selfie sticks for around $5; a “self-stirring mug.” By the end of 2015, though, these posts were appearing with striking frequency. That year, Wish’s parent company was reported to be one of the largest advertisers on Facebook and Instagram during the holiday season.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '70', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/07/magazine/07alibaba/07mag-07alibaba-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/07/magazine/07alibaba/07mag-07alibaba-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 394}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/07/magazine/07alibaba/07mag-07alibaba-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/07/magazine/07alibaba/07mag-07alibaba-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1345, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/07/magazine/07alibaba/07alibaba-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/07/magazine/07alibaba/07alibaba-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/07/magazine/07alibaba/07alibaba-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Online Marketplace That’s a Portal to the Future of Capitalism', 'kicker': 'The Money Issue', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Hookup', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wish (Mobile App)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-03T09:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Herrman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Herrman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6dbfe5c8-5a93-52a1-a543-7a12e4e0409b', 'word_count': 959, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6dbfe5c8-5a93-52a1-a543-7a12e4e0409b'}, {'abstract': 'How would you help a friend who had suicidal thoughts?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/03/learning/is-13-reasons-why-raising-awareness-about-teenage-suicide-or-glamorizing-it.html', 'snippet': 'How would you help a friend who had suicidal thoughts?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Have you ever had a friend who was severely depressed, or have you ever been badly depressed yourself? Have you heard about any teenagers whose depression led to attempted suicide, or who died from an attempt? In a private journal, write freely about your experiences with depression and teenage suicide.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{