t://article/6ad4492e-2139-5a2d-a21b-45e03a8ccfad', 'word_count': 147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ad4492e-2139-5a2d-a21b-45e03a8ccfad'}, {'abstract': 'Before photography, public events grand and small were often painted. This new exhibition shows an evolution of 18th-century history on canvas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/03/arts/design/eyewitness-views-at-the-getty-in-los-angeles-illustrates-history.html', 'snippet': 'Before photography, public events grand and small were often painted. This new exhibition shows an evolution of 18th-century history on canvas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Long before official photographers, painters were the artists most frequently assigned to depict public events grand and small. Volcanic eruptions, papal visits and the first hot-air balloon flight in Venice were documented by these masters, who often worked for hire. Opening on Tuesday, May 9, at the J. Paul Getty Museum in Los Angeles, “Eyewitness Views: Making History in Eighteenth Century Europe” is described by organizers as the first exhibition devoted to such contemporary views of history.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/07/arts/07GUIDE2/07GUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/07/arts/07GUIDE2/07GUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/07/arts/07GUIDE2/07GUIDE2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/07/arts/07GUIDE2/07GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 438, 'width': 600, 'subType