'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-03T14:17:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claire Cain Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claire', 'middlename': 'Cain', 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89a275c4-78bd-529e-b5b0-384c15ba4c80', 'word_count': 939, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89a275c4-78bd-529e-b5b0-384c15ba4c80'}, {'abstract': 'The new series hews closely to its predecessors before turning somber, in a very 21st-century way.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/03/arts/television/anne-with-an-e-on-netflix-reimagines-a-darker-green-gables.html', 'snippet': 'The new series hews closely to its predecessors before turning somber, in a very 21st-century way.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Anne of Green Gables,” Lucy Maud Montgomery’s adored 1908 novel about Anne Shirley, an 11-year-old Canadian orphan mistakenly placed in the care of the middle-age siblings Matthew and Marilla Cuthbert — they’d wanted a boy to work their Prince Edward Island farm — has been reimagined for the screen yet again, with the retitled “Anne With an E,” a collaboration with the CBC debuting Friday, May 12, on Netflix. Like her predecessors, this redheaded Anne (Amybeth McNulty) begins her new life as a spitfire and a romantic, chattering on in exclamatory sentences, thrilling at the beauty of apple trees and bridling at the notion of washing dishes. But soon the series turns somber in a very 21st-century (and perhaps more relatable) way, with bullying at the hands of Anne’s future husband, prompting the book’s smashed-slate scene, and flashbacks of abuse by her previous employers, who ultimately return her to the orphanage, where her only friend is her reflection in the glass. “I like imagining better than remembering,” Anne says.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/07/arts/07GUIDE1/07GUIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 854, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/07/arts/07GUIDE1/07GUIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 854}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/07/arts/07GUIDE1/07GUIDE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 720, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/07/arts/07GUIDE1/07GUIDE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2002, 'width': 1407, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/07/arts/07GUIDE1/07GUIDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/07/arts/07GUIDE1/07GUIDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/07/arts/07GUIDE1/07GUIDE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Anne With an E,’ on Netflix, Reimagines a Darker ‘Green Gables’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Television; Irrepressible Anne  Returns Yet Again', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations