o', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/04/us/04xp-tennessee_web1/04xp-tennessee_web1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1707, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/04/us/04xp-tennessee_web1/04xp-tennessee_web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/04/us/04xp-tennessee_web1/04xp-tennessee_web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/04/us/04xp-tennessee_web1/04xp-tennessee_web1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On Trail of Suspect, Bounty Hunters Killed an Innocent Man', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bounty Hunters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Clarksville (Tenn)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-04T02:43:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Haag', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haag', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4682b458-6c8d-5e31-80ab-94fd06b6f341', 'word_count': 354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4682b458-6c8d-5e31-80ab-94fd06b6f341'}, {'abstract': 'It takes impressive swagger for a show to spend an entire episode chasing a red herring. But the gamble pays off.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/03/arts/television/fargo-recap-the-law-of-non-contradiction.html', 'snippet': 'It takes impressive swagger for a show to spend an entire episode chasing a red herring. But the gamble pays off.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Mike Yanagita scene in the original “Fargo” is one of the most talked-about in the Coen brothers’ oeuvre, in part because it’s the one scene, in an otherwise airtight and intricate thriller, that isn’t critical to moving the action forward. (The other reason it’s brought up is to criticize the Coens for their condescension, but that’s not pertinent here.) The scene involves the police chief Marge Gunderson, who meets Yanagita, an old high school acquaintance, for a drink while she’s in Minneapolis investigating some bloody “malfeasance” in Brainerd, Minn. It’s an awkward encounter, in which Mike tearfully confesses his loneliness since the death of his wife and attempts to sidle up to Marge in a booth seat. Later, Marge learns that Mike’s wife is not dead — and that, in fact, he never had a wife at all.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/03/watching/03fargo/03fargo-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/03/watching/03fargo/03fargo-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/03/watching/03fargo/03fargo-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/03/watching/03fargo/03fargo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 393, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLar