nard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/428faf84-99cf-54f7-b1be-e81e7ddc5479', 'word_count': 695, 'uri': 'nyt://article/428faf84-99cf-54f7-b1be-e81e7ddc5479'}, {'abstract': 'The 1979 sci-fi horror film has left its mark on many films, from a “Friday the 13th” sequel to the newest “Alien” prequel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/04/movies/alien-covenant-influences.html', 'snippet': 'The 1979 sci-fi horror film has left its mark on many films, from a “Friday the 13th” sequel to the newest “Alien” prequel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has been 38 years since a terrifying alien burst from the chest of John Hurt in one of cinema’s most unforgettable scenes. And ever since, that creature — from the 1979 sci-fi scarefest “Alien,” about crew members of a spacecraft and the voracious organism they bring aboard — has continued to make its mark on the big screen. It’s now back in its old chomping grounds in “Alien: Covenant” (May 19), a prequel to the original.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '42', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How ‘Alien’ Spawned So Many Others', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How ‘Alien’ Spawned So Many Others', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Alien (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott, Ridley', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Alien: Covenant (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-04T17:39:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb043d8e-3648-5dad-a8fd-a699187c964d', 'word_count': 841, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb043d8e-3648-5dad-a8fd-a699187c964d'}, {'abstract': 'Also, shut out by a sister, drumming up dates, and going through the motions with a congregation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/04/fashion/social-qs-race-discrimination-at-work.html', 'snippet': 'Also, shut out by a sister, drumming up dates, and going through the motions with a congregation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I am a 30-year-old white guy. For three years, I have worked for a clothing company. My credentials are great: I graduated from an Ivy League college, I’ve been in fashion for my entire career, and my reviews have been excellent. But when the time came to replace our department manager, who transferred to another group, the company promoted a woman of color with a less impressive résumé (and four fewer months at the company) instead of me. I don’t want to accuse anyone of anything, but I feel demoralized. What should I do?', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'sub