s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The bodega is two aisles wide. Toward the back, where a piñata shaped like a giant frilly Negra Modelo beer bottle hangs by the ceiling vents, Pedro Rodriguez stands as studious as an apothecary, quietly filling plastic cups with shrimp, purplish nubs of octopus and a red liquid that looks lit from within. It is half cocktail, half remedy, a conjuring of Veracruz, Mexico, in Jackson Heights, Queens.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Shrimp Cocktail With a Jumbo Jolt, at La Esquina in Queens', 'kicker': 'Hungry City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Seafood Cocktails to Shock You Back to Life', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'La Esquina del Camaron Mexicano (Queens, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mexican Food (Cuisine)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jackson Heights (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-04T19:50:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ligaya Mishan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ligaya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mishan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f0dc591-4330-5171-ab17-41d697ce5e99', 'word_count': 759, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f0dc591-4330-5171-ab17-41d697ce5e99'}, {'abstract': 'Martha Schwendener and Will Heinrich select some of the best of the more than 200 galleries showing the wonderful, the curious — and the sure to be Instagrammed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/04/arts/design/frieze-new-york-art-fair.html', 'snippet': 'Martha Schwendener and Will Heinrich select some of the best of the more than 200 galleries showing the wonderful, the curious — and the sure to be Instagrammed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Frieze New York is a commitment. Now in its sixth year, with more than 200 galleries showing Modern and contemporary art from 30 countries, this fair is like a small city set up in a lavishly sculptural tent on Randalls Island. Yet its organizers have realized that visitors generally come for only one day. So this year Frieze is shorter, opening to the public on Friday and running through Sunday.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/05/arts/5FREIZECOVER1/5FREIZECOVER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/05/arts/5FREIZECOVER1/5FREIZECOVER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/05/arts/5FREIZECOVER1/5FREIZECOVER1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/05/arts/5FREIZECOVER1/5FREIZECOVER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/05/arts/5FREIZECOVER1/5FREIZECOVER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/05/arts/5FREIZECOVER1/5FREIZECOVER1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 769, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/05/arts/5FREIZECOVE