nytimes.com/2017/05/04/opinion/the-problem-of-pre-existing-conditions-goes-viral.html', 'snippet': 'The Republican proposal to limit coverage for those with pre-existing conditions has become the most emotional element of the health care debate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One vignette into how the debate over whether to repeal and replace the Affordable Care Act has touched a national nerve: A tweet of mine showing what could happen to premium costs for Americans with pre-existing conditions went viral two days ago, well beyond any of my previous tweets.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/04/opinion/rattner-contributor/rattner-contributor-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/10/04/opinion/rattner-contributor/rattner-contributor-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/04/opinion/rattner-contributor/rattner-contributor-jumbo-v4.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/04/opinion/rattner-contributor/rattner-contributor-superJumbo-v4.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/04/opinion/rattner-contributor/rattner-contributor-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/10/04/opinion/rattner-contributor/rattner-contributor-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/04/opinion/rattner-contributor/rattner-contributor-thumbLarge-v5.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Problem of Pre-existing Conditions Goes Viral', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-04T20:09:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Rattner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rattner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/15bda9b3-1a3d-5e0f-9cab-6180ed68e6ea', 'word_count': 105, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15bda9b3-1a3d-5e0f-9cab-6180ed68e6ea'}, {'abstract': 'This documentary, using footage shot by 40 filmmakers in 25 countries, depicts the uses and rituals of religion in a range of environments.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/04/movies/sacred-review.html', 'snippet': 'This documentary, using footage shot by 40 filmmakers in 25 countries, depicts the uses and rituals of religion in a range of environments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The TV journalist Bill Moyers once said of the mythologist Joseph Campbell that he “was one of the most spiritual men I ever met, but he didn’t have an ideology or a theology.” The same might be said of Thomas Lennon, who directed “Sacred,” a kaleidoscopic travelogue depicting demonstrations of faith worldwide. Mr. Lennon (no relation to the “Reno 911!” comedian) enlisted 40 filmmakers in 25 countries to record scenes large and small, and the results are surprisingly cohesive.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/05/arts/05sacred/05sacred-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/05/arts/05sacred/05sacred-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/05/arts/05sacred/05sacred-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/05/arts/05sacred/05sacred-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/05/arts/05sacred/05sacred-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/05/arts/05sacred/05sacred-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 580, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/05/arts/05sacred/05sacred-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1033, 'width': 1824, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Sacred,’ a Global Group Portrait of Faith in Action', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sacred', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Sacred (Movie)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lennon, Thomas F (Filmmaker)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-04T20:12:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1dfb82cb-0790-5abc-8567-54de3ae95c43', 'word_count': 266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1dfb82cb-0790-5abc-8567-54de3ae95c43'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Hekmatyar, an ex-prime minister who once helped destroy Kabul, has returned with immunity in hopes it will lead to talks with the Taliban.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/04/world/asia/afghan-warlord-returns-to-city-he-left-in-ruins-with-hope-for-peace.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Hekmatyar, an ex-prime minister who once helped destroy Kabul, has returned with immunity in hopes it will lead to talks with the Taliban.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — The last time Gulbuddin Hekmatyar, an Afghan warlord, was in Kabul more than 20 years ago, he was the prime minister and a participant in a factional war that destroyed the capital and claimed tens of thousands of lives.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/05/world/05hekmatyar1/05hekmatyar1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/05/world/05hekmatyar1/05hekmatyar1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/05/world/05