rivate-portrait-review.html', 'snippet': 'Though this documentary looks at the artist and his work, it is more concerned with layering on the admiration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No commercials are shown during “Julian Schnabel: A Private Portrait.” They would only be redundant. Instead this documentary serves as a feature-length advertisement for the artist, and is about as daring as a billboard for skim milk.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/05/arts/05Julian/05Julian-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/05/arts/05Julian/05Julian-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/05/arts/05Julian/05Julian-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/05/arts/05Julian/05Julian-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1151, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/05/arts/05Julian/05Julian-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/05/arts/05Julian/05Julian-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/05/arts/05Julian/05Julian-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Julian Schnabel: A Private Portrait’ Puts Praise Above Art', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Julian Schnabel: A Private Portrait', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schnabel, Julian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Julian Schnabel: A Private Portrait (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corsicato, Pappi', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-04T20:40:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Jaworowski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jaworowski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/97aef917-d052-5241-bfc8-61a4708fa9c0', 'word_count': 267, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97aef917-d052-5241-bfc8-61a4708fa9c0'}, {'abstract': 'This Italian comedy-drama tells an interesting, if not tasteful, story about polar opposites bonding in a mental institution.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/04/movies/like-crazy-review.html', 'snippet': 'This Italian comedy-drama tells an interesting, if not tasteful, story about polar opposites bonding in a mental institution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cultural sensitivity about mental illness has increased to the extent that using a psychiatric hospital or its residents as metaphors for society in general is considered in bad taste, at least. But either nobody has told this to the Italian film director Paolo Virzì, or he just doesn’t care. The analogy he draws between Italy and two initially opposed women in an institution is the linchpin of his “Like Crazy,” an energetic, visually attractive but ultimately irritating comedy-drama.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/05/arts/05LIKECRAZY/05LIKECRAZY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/05/arts/05LIKECRAZY/05LIKECRAZY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/05/arts/05LIKECRAZY/05LIKECRAZY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/05/arts/05LIKECRAZY/05LIKECRAZY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/05/arts/05LIKECRAZY/05LIKECRAZY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/05/arts/05LIKECRAZY/05LIKECRAZY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/05/arts/05LIKECRAZY/05LIKECRAZY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: In ‘Like Crazy,’ an Unlikely Pair Flee the Cuckoo’s Nest', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Like Crazy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Like Crazy (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Virzi, Paolo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bruni-Tedeschi, Valeria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ramazzotti, Micaela', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-04T20:43:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Glenn Kenny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/22948add-a4aa-5dc2-b4f6-89a5d0394d2f', 'word_count': 296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22948add-a4aa-5dc2-b4f6-89a5d0394d2f'}, {'abstract': 'Chris Pratt, Zoe Saldana and the crew are back for this sequel to the 2014 hit about a ragtag group of futuristic fighters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/04/movies/guardians-of-the-galaxy-2-review-chris-pratt.html', 'snippet': 'Chris Pratt, Zoe Saldana and the crew are back for this sequel to the 2014 hit about a ragtag group of futuristic fighters.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 2” has all the digital bells and whistles as well as much of the likable, self-aware waggery of the first. In many respects, it’s not much different except it all feels a bit strained, as if everyone were trying too hard, especially its writer-director, James Gunn. Most of the ragtag futuristic fighters who powered through Vol 1. three years ago are back on board and led by Peter Quill (Chris Pratt), a cheerily roguish type who calls himself Star-Lord. The name still brings a light smile, even if the movie can’t help but feel as deadly serious as any other lucratively branded Marvel property.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/05/arts/0505GUARDIANS1/0505GUARDIANS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 316, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/05/arts/0505GUARDIANS1/0505GUARDIANS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 316}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/05/arts/0505GUARDIANS1/0505GUARDIANS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 540, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/05/arts/0505GUARDIANS1/0505GUARDIANS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/05/arts/0505GUARDIANS1/0505GUARDIANS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/05/arts/0505GUARDIANS1/0505GUARDIANS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/05/arts/0505GUARDIANS1/0505GUARDIANS1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 2’ Wants That Loving Feeling', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Looking for That Loving Feeling', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Guardians of the Galaxy Vol 2 (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gunn, James (1970- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pratt, Chris', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saldana, Zoe', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': '