tions', 'value': 'New Victory Theater', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-05T14:42:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corey Kilgannon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Corey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kilgannon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17fe6fb8-bbd0-50bb-8203-bc19a3a6ab81', 'word_count': 1137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17fe6fb8-bbd0-50bb-8203-bc19a3a6ab81'}, {'abstract': 'Alissa J. Rubin, the Paris bureau chief, discovered that campaign stops for a French presidential candidate can be a bit different from those for an American one.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/05/insider/on-the-mountain-top-with-a-french-presidential-candidate.html', 'snippet': 'Alissa J. Rubin, the Paris bureau chief, discovered that campaign stops for a French presidential candidate can be a bit different from those for an American one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PAU, FRANCE — Not surprisingly it’s very different to travel with a French presidential candidate than with an American one. Granted, this was not an ordinary trip for Emmanuel Macron, the centrist candidate for president of France, but still. We (myself and the French photographer, Pierre Terdjman) took a flight at dawn down to Pau, which is inland from Biarritz and in the plains just below where the Pyrenees begin. There we joined with a press pool following Mr. Macron.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/03/world/03-insider-france/03-insider-france-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/03/world/03-insid