'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Colicchio, Tom', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-05T16:45:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Well', 'section_name': 'Well', 'subsection_name': 'Eat', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Saint Louis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': 'Saint', 'lastname': 'Louis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0493983-7dfd-5754-b1d7-77da98a8b58a', 'word_count': 620, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0493983-7dfd-5754-b1d7-77da98a8b58a'}, {'abstract': 'On the eve of a gala celebrating the company’s anniversary at Lincoln Center, our critic asks how its grand home relates to its artistic challenges.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/05/arts/music/is-the-met-opera-too-big-and-other-questions-as-its-home-turns-50.html', 'snippet': 'On the eve of a gala celebrating the company’s anniversary at Lincoln Center, our critic asks how its grand home relates to its artistic challenges.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When an opera company moves into a new home, there’s always lingering nostalgia for the old one. But fans of the Metropolitan Opera were more than ready to vacate the worn old Met at 39th Street and Broadway for a massive new theater at Lincoln Center. The old Met, I vaguely remember from attending a few performances as a teenager, had fine acoustics and, with its golden horseshoe interior, a kind of faded, dusty grandeur. But backstage resources were woefully inadequate.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/07/arts/07METFIFTY2/07METFIFTY2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 473, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/07/arts/07METFIFTY2/07METFIFTY2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 473}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/07/arts/07METFIFTY2/07METFIFTY2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 808, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/07/arts/07METFIFTY2/07METFIFTY2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1616, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/07/arts/07METFIFTY2/07METFIFTY2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/07/arts/07METFIFTY2/07METFIFTY2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/07/arts/07METFIFTY2/07METFIFTY2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Is the Met Opera Too Big? And Other Questions as Its Home Turns 50', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Is the Met Opera Too Big?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-05T16:45:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6b31707-403f-594d-a8d0-699c1880c7b7', 'word_count': 1205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6b31707-403f-594d-a8d0-699c1880c7b7'}, {'abstract': 'As the Metropolitan Opera celebrates its 50th year at Lincoln Center, we crunch the numbers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/05/arts/music/triumph-tragedy-and-50000-hats-the-met-opera-by-the-numbers.html', 'snippet': 'As the Metropolitan Opera celebrates its 50th year at Lincoln Center, we crunch the numbers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Metropolitan Opera moved to Lincoln Center from Broadway at 39th Street in 1966, a subway token cost 20 cents, the Supremes’s “You Can’t Hurry Love” was at the top of the Billboard charts, and the (pre-miracle) Mets were wrapping up their fifth season. Since then, a lot of sopranos have gone on to meet tragic but beautiful-sounding ends. As the Met prepares to celebrate its 50th anniversary at Lincoln Center with an all-star gala on Sunday, May 7, here is a look at its first half-century in its new home — by the numbers.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/07/arts/07metfifty-side/07metfifty-side-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/07/arts/07metfifty-side/07metfifty-side-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/07/arts/07metfifty-side/07metfifty-side-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/07/arts/07metfifty-side/07metfifty-side-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/07/arts/07metfifty-side/07metfifty-side-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/07/arts/07metfifty-side/07metfifty-side-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/07/arts/07metfifty-side/07metfifty-side-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Triumph, Tragedy and 50,000 Hats: The Met Opera by the Numbers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Triumph and Tragedy by the Numbers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levine, James', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-05T16:45:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2c1836b-135d-583b-8bca-65e4d4fb0167', 'word_count': 883, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2c1836b-135d-583b-8bca-65e4d4fb0167'}, {'abstract': 'Moira proves to be the inspiration Offred needs to resist the strictures of Gilead.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/05/arts/television/handmaids-tale-recap-nolite-te-bastardes-carborundorum.html', 'snippet': 'Moira proves to be the inspiration Offred needs to resist the strictures of Gilead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Memory can be a weapon or a wound, it’s all a matter of perspective. As Offred struggles with nearly two weeks of imprisonment in her room, her memories soon appear to be both. Her memories of the time she, Luke and Hannah went to a carnival prove to be a potent refuge. But Offred tries not to linger in the past, worried it will only compound her fragile mental state. It’s too easy to get lost remembering the way things were rather than grappling with the present.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/03/watching/03handmaid4/03handmaid4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/03/watching/03handmaid4/03handmaid4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/03/watching/03handmaid4/03handmaid4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/03/watching/03handmaid4/03handmaid4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/03/watching/03handmaid4/03handmaid4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/03/watching/03handmaid4/03handmaid4-jumbo.jpg', 'height'