he tabloid glare as willingly and relentlessly as Caitlyn Jenner has, a memoir might seem greedy, or at least redundant. What can be left to overshare? Still, here comes a Jenner memoir with the tattletale title “The Secrets of My Life” (written with Buzz Bissinger and new at No. 8 in hardcover nonfiction), and it turns out to be plenty revealing. Jenner discusses her ambivalence at becoming a macho role model after winning decathlon gold as Bruce Jenner, along with her early experiences cross-dressing and her attempts to reconcile her gender identity in a succession of doomed marriages. She also relates a funny anecdote about appearing on a Bob Hope television special after the Olympics, for a skit that required dressing in drag. “I have to be careful not to show too much enthusiasm, so I play it cool," she remembers. “Our wigs and dresses are purposely ridiculous. But the red heels I think not only look good on me but also fit, so I steal them after the show.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '36', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/books/review/14list/14list-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 612, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/14/books/review/14list/14list-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 612}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/books/review/14list/14list-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 880, 'width': 863, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/books/review/14list/14list-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 880, 'width': 863, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'imag