ion': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbc4f80f-a287-570d-a0ee-df4e59d37a12', 'word_count': 1191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbc4f80f-a287-570d-a0ee-df4e59d37a12'}, {'abstract': 'Readers were quick to point out that a headline fell short in conveying the potential impact of the Republican health care bill.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/05/public-editor/healthcare-republicans-poor-headline-liz-spayd.html', 'snippet': 'Readers were quick to point out that a headline fell short in conveying the potential impact of the Republican health care bill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the House of Representatives passed the Republican health care bill Thursday, The New York Times was quick to publish a sidebar that mapped out the bill’s potential impact on individuals. The winners? The wealthy and upper middle class. The losers? The poor and elderly.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/06/opinion/06pubed-art/06pubed-art-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 388, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/06/opinion/06pubed-art/06pubed-art-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 388}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/06/opinion/06pubed-art/06pubed-art-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 662, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/06/opinion/06pubed-art/06pubed-art-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1324, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/06/opinion/06pubed-art/06pubed-art-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/06/opinion/06pubed-art/06pubed-art-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/06/opinion/06pubed-art/06pubed-art-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Story Was Fine, the Headline Less So', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-05T19:38:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Public Editor', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Spayd', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spayd', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/986bf2ca-410b-568d-a6b7-d0140d37dce8', 'word_count': 251, 'uri': 'nyt://article/986bf2ca-410b-568d-a6b7-d0140d37dce8'}, {'abstract': 'The only way to make premiums affordable for most people is to limit excessive cost-sharing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/05/opinion/what-the-republican-health-plan-gets-right.html', 'snippet': 'The only way to make premiums affordable for most people is to limit excessive cost-sharing.', 'lead_pa