/moonlit-handel-this-weeks-8-best-classical-music-moments.html', 'snippet': 'Music by Andrew Norman, Beethoven\'s Ninth and "Der Rosenkavalier" at the Met Opera were among the highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In addition to reviews, features and news during the week, our critics and reporters collect the best of what they’ve heard: notes that sent shivers down their spines, memorable voices, quotations that cut to the heart of the story.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Moonlit Handel: This Week’s 8 Best Classical Music Moments', 'kicker': 'That decisive moment', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Norman, Andrew (1979- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Philharmonic', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Opera', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'MATA Festival', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Blue Heron (Music Group)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NYC Master Chorale', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-05T21:40:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17a166be-c446-5bd5-9db1-c0d41c9f036a', 'word_count': 902, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17a166be-c446-5bd5-9db1-c0d41c9f036a'}, {'abstract': 'C. E. Morgan’s “The Sport of Kings,” William Nack’s “Secretariat” and other books to read on the first Saturday in May.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/05/books/5-books-to-read-on-kentucky-derby-day.html', 'snippet': 'C. E. Morgan’s “The Sport of Kings,” William Nack’s “Secretariat” and other books to read on the first Saturday in May.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To get a handle on which horse to bet among the 20 entrants in tomorrow’s Kentucky Derby, turn to The Times’s Joe Drape and Melissa Hoppert. While they were busy handicapping the field, I was turning, as I usually do at this time of year, to my fairly robust shelf of books about the sport. Assuming you’re already familiar with Laura Hillenbrand’s best-selling “Seabiscuit” (and if not, then with its film adaptation), here are a handful of other books to read on Derby Day, and during the rest of the Triple Crown season that follows it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/05/books/05horse-covers/05horse-covers-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 173, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/05/books/05horse-covers/05horse-covers-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 173}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/05/books/05horse-covers/05horse-covers-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 296, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/05/books/05horse-covers/05horse-covers-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 355, 'width': 1229, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/05/books/05horse-covers/05horse-covers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/05/books/05horse-covers/05horse-covers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/05/books/05horse-covers/05horse-covers-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '5 Books to Read on Kentucky Derby Day', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-05T21:43:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e36dcbf3-33f4-5a4a-90d1-eb0925519883', 'word_count': 525, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e36dcbf3-33f4-5a4a-90d1-eb0925519883'}, {'abstract': 'The House’s vote to repeal Obamacare has extended to Montana’s special congressional election, in which the Republican nominee had, at first, tried to distance himself from the measure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/05/us/politics/montana-house-special-election-greg-gianforte-health-bill.html', 'snippet': 'The House’s vote to repeal Obamacare has extended to Montana’s special congressional election, in which the Republican nominee had, at first, tried to distance himself from the measure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — When Greg Gianforte, the Republican running for an open House seat in Montana, was asked on Thursday whether he would have supported the bill repealing the Affordable Care Act that passed the House that day, he declined to answer.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_pag