into Vietnam.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/05/opinion/leaving-college-going-to-war.html', 'snippet': 'Fifty years ago, I was about to graduate — and get drafted into Vietnam.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Much as the Blue Ridge Mountains towered over campus, “Vietnam” loomed constantly in the background that spring, exactly 50 years ago, when 264 classmates and I were preparing to graduate from the all-male, almost all-white Washington & Lee University in Lexington, Va. Next door at the Virginia Military Institute, where the graduates would automatically become commissioned officers, Vietnam loomed even larger.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/06/opinion/06nicklin-vietnam1web/06nicklin-vietnam1web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/06/opinion/06nicklin-vietnam1web/06nicklin-vietnam1web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/06/opinion/06nicklin-vietnam1web/06nicklin-vietnam1web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/06/opinion/06nicklin-vietnam1web/06nicklin-vietnam1web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/06/opinion/06nicklin-vietnam1web/06nicklin-vietnam1web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/06/opinion/06nicklin-vietnam1web/06nicklin-vietnam1web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1024, 'sub