d am ready to go.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day: Senate Panel Asks Trump Associates for Communications With Russians', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quote of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2017-05-06T00:58:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Today’s Paper', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa4786d1-94ce-5700-81af-9910e8c4978a', 'word_count': 53, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa4786d1-94ce-5700-81af-9910e8c4978a'}, {'abstract': 'As a White House official, Ms. Trump may send the wrong signal by plugging “Women Who Work” on Instagram and Twitter, but violates no laws, ethics experts said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/05/business/ivanka-trump-book.html', 'snippet': 'As a White House official, Ms. Trump may send the wrong signal by plugging “Women Who Work” on Instagram and Twitter, but violates no laws, ethics experts said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ivanka Trump will continue to promote her new book on Twitter and Instagram, according to a spokeswoman, weeks after President Trump’s adviser and daughter pledged not to draw publicity through a promotional tour or media appearances.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ivanka Trump Promotes Her Book on Social Media (but Not in the Media)', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ivanka Trump Promotes Her New Book on Social Media (Though Not in the Media)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Ivanka', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics and Official Misconduct', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conflicts of Interest'