'abstract': 'He skipped a party. It was a good step.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/06/opinion/sunday/when-trump-knows-enough-to-stay-home.html', 'snippet': 'He skipped a party. It was a good step.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The White House Correspondents Dinner is one of the most repulsive social events in Washington. And you should go once, if you get the chance. You are packed like sardines into the 1950s-style basement ballroom of the “Hinckley” Hilton (where Ronald Reagan was shot), eating hotel-banquet food and trying to be heard above the din, while the person you’re talking to looks over your shoulder for someone more important.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/07/opinion/sunday/07kinsley/07kinsley-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/07/opinion/sunday/07kinsley/07kinsley-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/07/opinion/sunday/07kinsley/07kinsley-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/07/opinion/sunday/07kinsley/07kinsley-articleLarge.gif', 'height': 463, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/07/opinion/sunday/07kinsley/07kinsley-articleLarge.gif', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 463}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/07/opinion/sunday/07kinsley/07kinsley-jumbo.gif', 'height': 790, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/07/opinion/sunday/07kinsley/07kinsley-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 806, 'width': 1083, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Trump Knows Enough to Stay Home', 'kicker': 'Opinion | Say Something Nice About Donald Trump', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trump Knows Enough to Stay Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-06T18:30:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Kinsley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kinsley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7aa0f21-6799-5c3d-94f2-4c2f6070e10a', 'word_count': 550, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7aa0f21-6799-5c3d-94f2-4c2f6070e10a'}, {'abstract': 'With some 163 of their colleagues in jail, the men and women of news media are understandably fearful.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/06/opinion/sunday/a-celebration-turns-into-a-somber-recitation-of-jailed-turkish-journalists.html', 'snippet': 'With some 163 of their colleagues in jail, the men and women of news media are understandably fearful.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISTANBUL — With some 163 of their fellow journalists in jail, the men and women of Turkey’s news media are understandably fearful. Many of those who avoided prison as part of President Recep Tayyip Erdogan’s sweeping crackdown on alleged enemies after a July coup attempt have lost their jobs at media outlets taken over by Mr. Erdogan’s cronies. Some of