can grooves.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/07/arts/music/angelique-kidjo-remain-in-light-talking-heads.html', 'snippet': 'The 1980 Talking Heads album that embraced music from the African diaspora gets an update with new African grooves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Africa rapturously reclaimed rock when Angélique Kidjo, from Benin, performed all the songs from Talking Heads’ album “Remain in Light” on Friday night at Carnegie Hall, along with a few of her own. She plans to tour with “Remain in Light,” and is recording the songs as a studio album with a top pop producer, Jeff Bhasker. From the stage, she declared, “I always as an artist want to try to find a way to create bridges between cultures.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/08/arts/08KIDJO1/08KIDJO1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/08/arts/08KIDJO1/08KIDJO1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/08/arts/08KIDJO1/08KIDJO1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/08/arts/08KIDJO1/08KIDJO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/08/arts/08KIDJO1/08KIDJO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/08/arts/08KIDJO1/08KIDJO1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legac