r seemed “so old-fashioned.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'MILAN — From the creation of Fondazione Prada to underwriting creative exhibits across the globe, Miuccia Prada has long made a point of walking the line between fashion and art. So it was fitting that her first stand-alone cruise collection show was held in the Osservatorio, the foundation’s new photography gallery nestled under the glass and iron domes of the Galleria Vittorio Emanuele II, where Prada opened its first store in 1913. And that the show was held on Sunday, just before the glamorous whirl of the opening parties for the Venice Biennale this week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/11/fashion/11OTRprada/08pradacruise-A-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/11/fashion/11OTRprada/08pradacruise-A-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/11/fashion/11OTRprada/08pradacruise-A-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/11/fashion/11OTRprada/08pradacruise-A-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/11/fashion/11OTRprada/08pradacruise-A-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/11/fashion/11OTRprada/08pradacruise-A-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'cr