, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff53a543-d60e-5c94-872c-d9bfbf6c6c00', 'word_count': 634, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff53a543-d60e-5c94-872c-d9bfbf6c6c00'}, {'abstract': 'I have seen the worst the world can offer. That’s why I believe the United States needs to protect what is good.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/08/opinion/john-mccain-rex-tillerson-human-rights.html', 'snippet': 'I have seen the worst the world can offer. That’s why I believe the United States needs to protect what is good.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Washington, D.C. — SOME years ago, I heard Natan Sharansky, the human rights icon, recount how he and his fellow refuseniks in the Soviet Union took renewed courage from statements made on their behalf by President Ronald Reagan. Word had reached the gulag that the leader of the most powerful nation on earth had spoken in defense of their right to self-determination. America, personified by its president, gave them hope, and hope is a powerful defense against oppression.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/08/opinion/08mccain/08mccain-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/08/opinion/08mccain/08mccain-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/08/opinion/08mccain/08mccain-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/08/opinion/08mccain/08mccain-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1800, 'width': 1800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/08/opinion/08mccain/08mccain-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/08/opinion/08mccain/08mccain-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/08/opinion/08mccain/08mccain-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'John McCain: Why We Must Support Human Rights', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'We Must Support Human Rights', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tillerson, Rex W', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-08T07:21:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By John McCain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McCain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f54035ff-6e0c-55d5-b9ef-b3af1796e41c', 'word_count': 815, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f54035ff-6e0c-55d5-b9ef-b3af1796e41c'}, {'abstract': 'Making policy by lying about everything.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/08/opinion/republicans-party-like-its-1984.html', 'snippet': 'Making policy by lying about everything.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There have been many bad laws in U.S. history. Some bills were poorly conceive