Incan estate as a day trip from Cuzco requires extra preparation, but you can do it, unrushed.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Was it worth it?” That’s the most common question I’ve fielded since I visited Machu Picchu, the ruins of a 15th-century Incan estate that sit almost 8,000 feet above sea level. Thrust back into prominence when the American explorer Hiram Bingham “discovered” it in 1911, it was used, by some accounts, as a palace, a retreat for the wealthy, a religious sanctuary or all three. Today, the photo-friendly ruins (popular with tourists and Obamas alike) receive thousands of visitors daily and are the engine that drives Peru’s tourism industry.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/travel/14FRUGAL/14FRUGAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 728, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/14/travel/14FRUGAL/14FRUGAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 728}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/travel/14FRUGAL/14FRUGAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 844, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/travel/14FRUGAL/14FRUGAL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1688, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/travel/14FRUGAL/14FRUGAL-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/14/travel/14FRUGAL/14FRUGAL-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/travel/14FRUGAL/14FRUGAL-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Conquering Machu Picchu, the Cheap and Quick Way', 'kicker': 'Frugal Traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Machu Picchu, With Little Money and Less Time', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Machu Picchu (Peru)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budget Travel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hikes and Hiking', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-08T14:44:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lucas Peterson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lucas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Peterson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8832b8c2-0e89-55a5-a762-52c8dfded819', 'word_count': 1238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8832b8c2-0e89-55a5-a762-52c8dfded819'}, {'abstract': 'A new kitchen timer bursts into the composer’s Piano Sonata No. 11 when it’s time to check on the food.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/08/dining/kikkerland-kitchen-timer-mozart.html', 'snippet': 'A new kitchen timer bursts into the composer’s Piano Sonata No. 11 when it’s time to check on the food.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Banish the insistent oven buzz. A new cooking timer alerts the cook when the cake is done with a few bars of Mozart. The gadget, topped with a bust of the composer, bursts into the lilting Rondo alla Turca, the third movement of his Piano Sonata No. 11, when the time is up; it should cheer a highbrow cook for Mother’s Day: Mozart Kitchen Timer, $17.50, Kikkerland Shop, 493 Avenue of the Americas (13th Street), 212-262-5000, kikkerland.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/10/dining/10BURNER-TIMER/10BURNER-TIMER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/10/dining/10BURNER-TIMER/10BURNER-TIMER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/10/dining/10BURNER-TIMER/10BURNER-TIMER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/10/dining/10BURNER-TIMER/10BURNER-TIMER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/10/dining/10BURNER-TIMER/10BURNER-TIMER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/10/dining/10BURNER-TIMER/10BURNER-TIMER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/10/dining/10BURNER-TIMER/10BURNER-TIMER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Mozart Melody for the Master Chef', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Serenade: Timer Trades the Buzzing For a Fine Mozart Melody', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': '