ba6-bcad-3d1b37a9c9d0'}, {'abstract': 'CompStat will send New Yorkers questions on their smartphones to see if they feel safe, if they trust the police and if they are confident in the department.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/08/nyregion/nypd-compstat-crime-mapping.html', 'snippet': 'CompStat will send New Yorkers questions on their smartphones to see if they feel safe, if they trust the police and if they are confident in the department.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was a policing invention with a futuristic sounding name — CompStat — when the New York Police Department introduced it as a management system for fighting crime in an era of much higher violence in the 1990s. Police departments around the country, and the world, adapted its system of mapping muggings, robberies and other crimes; measuring police activity; and holding local commanders accountable.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/09/nyregion/09COMPSTAT1/00METER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/09/nyregion/09COMPSTAT1/00METER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 404}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/09/nyregion/09COMPSTAT1/00METER1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 690, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/09/nyregion/09COMPSTAT1/00METER1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1380, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/09/nyregion/09COMPSTAT1/00METER1-thumbStandard.jpg',