f the war effort.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/09/us/09opinion/09opinion-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/09/us/09opinion/09opinion-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/09/us/09opinion/09opinion-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/09/us/09opinion/09opinion-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 430, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/09/us/09opinion/09opinion-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 430}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/09/us/09opinion/09opinion-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 733, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/09/us/09opinion/09opinion-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1074, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Johnson, Westmoreland and the ‘Selling’ of Vietnam', 'kicker': "Vietnam '67", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vietnam War', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Westmoreland, William C', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Lyndon Baines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vietnam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-09T07:21:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gregory Daddis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gregory', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Daddis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/06e6a128-7062-5a20-a10d-2e2a9f1219c0', 'word_count': 1366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06e6a128-7062-5a20-a10d-2e2a9f1219c0'}, {'abstract': 'Remaining in the treaty would spur new investment, strengthen American competitiveness, create jobs and ensure access to global markets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/09/opinion/the-business-case-for-the-paris-climate-accord.html', 'snippet': 'Remaining in the treaty would spur new investment, strengthen American competitiveness, create jobs and ensure access to global markets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Trump faces a choice that will echo across his presidency and beyond: whether to remain in the Paris climate agreement. Although most Americans, his own secretaries of state and energy, and heads of state from around the globe are urging the president to stay, he remains undecided. Let us hope that a newly invigorated pro-Paris campaign by many of America’s top C.E.O.s will sway him.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/09/opinion/09schultzWeb/09schultzWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/09/opinion/09schultzWeb/09schultzWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 405}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/09/opinion/09schultzWeb/09schultzWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'hei