{'abstract': 'Their cause — a fight for decent, secure wages and comprehensive benefits — has implications for the entire labor market.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/09/opinion/why-yale-graduate-students-are-on-a-hunger-strike.html', 'snippet': 'Their cause — a fight for decent, secure wages and comprehensive benefits — has implications for the entire labor market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW HAVEN, Conn. — Two weeks ago, Yale graduate student teachers began a hunger strike to pressure the school to negotiate with their union. Eight committed to fasting, planning only to stop if a doctor says their health is at risk of permanent damage. If a student has to stop fasting, another union member takes his or her spot. Four of the students have had nothing but water for 14 days.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/08/opinion/yalehunger_1/yalehunger_1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/08/opinion/yalehunger_1/yalehunger_1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/08/opinion/yalehunger_1/yalehunger_1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/08/opinion/yalehunger_1/yalehunger_1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 325, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/08/opinion/yalehunger_1/yalehunger_1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 325}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/08/opinion/yalehunger_1/yalehunger_1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 555, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/08/opinion/yalehunger_1/yalehunger_1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1110, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Yale Graduate Students Are on a Hunger Strike', 'kicker': 'On Campus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Graduate Schools and Students', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hunger Strikes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collective Bargaining', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tenure', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Labor Relations Board', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Salovey, Peter', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-09T15:10:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/51ea7cc7-3c9b-5835-876c-d39dff297360', 'word_count': 984, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51ea7cc7-3c9b-5835-876c-d39dff297360'}, {'abstract': 'The victory of Mr. Moon, a liberal, could open a rift with the United States over how to best contain North Korea’s nuclear arsenal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/0