tus quo and avoid possible hostilities with North Korea, while President Trump wants to apply maximum pressure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/09/world/asia/south-korea-election-north-korea-trump-moon-jae-in.html', 'snippet': 'Moon Jae-in wants to maintain the status quo and avoid possible hostilities with North Korea, while President Trump wants to apply maximum pressure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The last time an American president decided to squeeze North Korea hard to abandon its nuclear weapons program, cutting off a bank in Macau where its top leaders secretly stashed their cash, the effort worked brilliantly — until South Korea’s president complained to George W. Bush that it had to stop.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/10/world/10TRUMPKOREA/10TRUMPKOREA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/10/world/10TRUMPKOREA/10TRUMPKOREA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 391}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/10/world/10TRUMPKOREA/10TRUMPKOREA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/10/world/10TRUMPKOREA/10TRUMPKOREA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1334, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/10/world/10TRUMPKOREA/10TRUMPKOREA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/10/world/10TRUMPKOREA/10T