ippet': 'A flurry of announcements — including a cash infusion from KKR, new board members and widening losses — sets the stage for a sale of the company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pandora is shuffling to find a profitable tune. The streaming-music service is getting a $150 million injection from the private-equity firm KKR. It is also shaking up its board and exploring a sale as it struggles to stem losses and get listeners to pay. With Spotify dominating subscriptions, Pandora has little choice.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pandora, Digital Music Pioneer, Is Running Out of Options', 'kicker': 'Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Spotify', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Audio Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pandora Media Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kkr & Company LP', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-09T18:33:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Saba', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saba', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7929056a-77e7-5678-8aa7-b3e1f77c6980', 'word_count': 415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7929056a-77e7-5678-8aa7-b3e1f77c6980'}, {'abstract': 'Pirates, aliens and lifeguards come to the big screen this month.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/09/movies/summer-movie-trailers-may-2017.html', 'snippet': 'Pirates, aliens and lifeguards come to the big screen this month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After two revisionist takes on Sherlock Holmes, the director Guy Ritchie aims to show off the hipper side of King Arthur, a character whose last major reboot was in a 2004 Antoine Fuqua film. An irreverent Charlie Hunnam plays the title role; Jude Law is the pretender to Arthur’s rightful throne.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Watch 10 Trailers for May', 'kicker': 'Summer movies', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-09T18:48:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Kenigsberg and Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenigsberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/944a1fef-4586-5b28-91fc-9d2ad42f8379', 'word_count': 577, 'uri': 'nyt://article/944a1fef-4586-5b28-91fc-9d2ad42f8379'}, {'abstract': 'In “The Ghost Festival” at Danspace Project, his first solo show, Koma pays homage to his dance ancestors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/09/arts/dance/koma-alone-except-for-all-the-dancing-spirits-in-the-room.html', 'snippet': 'In “The Ghost Festival” at Danspace Project, his first solo show, Koma pays homage to his dance ancestors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Koma Otake has been dealing with a foot injury for nearly a decade. So some show-and-tell was in order on a recent Sunday. In a parked car in the East Village, he took off his shoes and socks to display his ankles to a reporter.', 'print_section'