ifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1382901c-6408-5720-bfb8-b703c30ddcea', 'word_count': 965, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1382901c-6408-5720-bfb8-b703c30ddcea'}, {'abstract': 'In his first public foray abroad since leaving office, Mr. Obama linked climate and food issues and met with Matteo Renzi, the former Italian prime minister seeking a comeback.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/09/world/europe/obama-food-milan-seeds-chips.html', 'snippet': 'In his first public foray abroad since leaving office, Mr. Obama linked climate and food issues and met with Matteo Renzi, the former Italian prime minister seeking a comeback.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — Barack Obama took his first step back onto the world stage on Tuesday, shedding his tie to give wide-ranging, if studiously nonpartisan, remarks during a food and technology conference in Milan.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/10/world/10obama/1obama-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 424, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/10/world/10obama/1obama-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 424}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/10/world/10obama/1obama-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 724, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/10/world/10obama/1obama-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1447, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017