rd_count': 712, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93b3f9f7-ba00-5467-b931-3debaa06e030'}, {'abstract': 'Rejecting a video that Israel said showed the Palestinian leader Marwan Barghouti cheating on his hunger strike, Fadwa Barghouti said the protest was gaining momentum.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/09/world/middleeast/marwan-barghouti-hunger-strike-palestinians-israel.html', 'snippet': 'Rejecting a video that Israel said showed the Palestinian leader Marwan Barghouti cheating on his hunger strike, Fadwa Barghouti said the protest was gaining momentum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RAMALLAH, West Bank — Truth in the Middle East often boils down to what side you are on. To Fadwa Barghouti, the video that Israeli officials released this week was clearly fake: the one the Israelis said showed her husband, Marwan, the leader of a Palestinian hunger strike, furtively snacking in solitary confinement.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wife of Palestinian Hunger Striker Denies He’s Sneaking Food', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barghouti, Marwan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hunger Strikes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solitary Confinement', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ramallah (West Bank)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-09T20:04:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Fisher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fisher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5dd8f721-161f-5db5-acf4-027cd45cd979', 'word_count': 540, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5dd8f721-161f-5db5-acf4-027cd45cd979'}, {'abstract': 'Harvey, who was suspended for three days by the team, admitted he had been out late Friday night and played golf Saturday morning before missing that night’s game.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/09/sports/baseball/mets-matt-harvey-agology-suspension.html', 'snippet': 'Harvey, who was suspended for three days by the team, admitted he had been out late Friday night and played golf Saturday morning before missing that night’s game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Matt Harvey, battered and beleaguered, walked into the media room at Citi Field on Tuesday afternoon with his head down and sat down in front of the microphone.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/10/sports/10submets2/10submets2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/10/sports/10submets2/10submets2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/10/sports/10submets2/10submets2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/10/sports/10submets2/10submets2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 453, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/10/sports/10submets2/10submets2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 453}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/10/sports/10submets2/10submets2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 772, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/10/sports/10submets2/10submets2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1378, 'width': 1827, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With Head Down, a Contrite Matt Harvey Apologizes to His Mets Teammates', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Not for the First Time, Harvey Apologizes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harvey, Matt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Apologies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-09T20:06:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Wagner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wagner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a8e3548-4476-5f75-b329-dd7fd21a4490', 'word_count': 1041, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a8e3548-4476-5f75-b329-dd7fd21a4490'}, {'abstract': 'David Garrow’s deeply reported “Rising Star” presents the 44th president as subordinating crucial parts of his life — even love — to political expedience.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/09/books/review/rising-star-biography-barack-obama-david-garrow.html', 'snippet': 'David Garrow’s deeply reported “Rising Star” presents the 44th president as subordinating crucial parts of his life — even love — to political expedience.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Barack Obama vexed his biographers by beating them to his origin story. His memoir “Dreams From My Father” — published in 1995 and reissued a decade later — locked down the narrative of how the son of a white American mother and an absent African father struggled for self-understanding until he embraced an African-American identity and married Michelle Robinson, a charismatic Harvard Law School graduate like himself and a member of Chicago’s small and insular black elite. Critics have often pointed to misstatements, errors of fact and composite characterizations in the book without impeaching its central narrative. But the historian David J. Garrow takes a hard line in “Rising Star: The Making of Barack Obama.” This impressive if gratuitously snarly biography is clearly intended to break the 44th president’s monopoly on his personal narrative.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/21/books/review/21Staples/21Staples-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/21/books/review/21Staples/21Staples-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/21/books/review/21Staples/21Staples-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/21/books/review/21Staples/21Staples-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 885, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/21/books/review/21Staples/21Staples-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 885}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/21/books/review/21Staples/21Staples-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 695, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/21/books/review/21Staples/21Staples-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1150, 'width': 780, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Take-No-Prisoners Biography of Barack Obama Examines His Early Love Life', 'kicker': 'Nonfiction', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Portrait of Obama as a Young Man', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garrow, David J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Rising Star: The Making of Barack Obama (Book)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-09T20:25:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brent Staples', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brent', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Staples', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c1ab7b5-3c18-524e-99d1-c1f256f82aad', 'word_count': 1220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c1ab7b5-3c18-524e-99d1-c1f256f82aad'}, {'abstract': 'Julian Rosefeldt’s art installation is now a film, with this chameleonic actress morphing into multiple characters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/09/movies/manifesto-review-cate-blanchett.html', 'snippet': 'Julian Rosefeldt’s art installation is now a film, with this chameleonic actress morphing into multiple characters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Movies adapted from art installations rarely come off well, even when the artwork has a strong cinematic element. Julian Rosefeldt’s “Manifesto,” which originated as an art installation, has toured the world, recently roosting at the Park Avenue Armory in Manhattan. It consists of filmed readings of various artistic and political manifestoes, dating from Marx and Engels’s 1848 “Communist Manifesto” and moving through the 20th century to Dada, Fluxus and even Lars von Trier’s Dogme 95 rules for filmmaking.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/10/arts/10MANIFESTO1/10MANIFESTO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/10/arts/10MANIFESTO1/10MANIFESTO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/10/arts/10MANIFESTO1/10MANIFESTO1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/10/arts/10MANIFESTO1/10MANIFESTO1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/10/arts/10MANIFESTO1/10MANIFESTO1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/10/arts/10MANIFESTO1/10MANIFESTO1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/10/arts/10MANIFESTO1/10MANIFESTO1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Cate Blanchett in ‘Manifesto,’ a Cerebral Exercise', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Ensemble Cast With One Face', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Manifesto (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosefeldt, Julian (1965- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blanchett, Cate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Manifesto (Exhibit)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-09T20:26:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Glenn Kenny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6d0846a-a1eb-5180-b57d-f9353757fecd', 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6d0846a-a1eb-5180-b57d-f9353757fecd'}, {'abstract': 'With the Trump administration still undecided about the Paris climate accord, Secretary of State Rex W. Tillerson is to head to a meeting of the Arctic Council in Alaska.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/09/climate/arctic-nations-to-meet-amid-unsettled-us-stance-on-climate-change.html', 'snippet': 'With the Trump administration still undecided about the Paris climate accord, Secretary of State Rex W. Tillerson is to head to a meeting of the Arctic Council in Alaska.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FAIRBANKS, Alaska — As Secretary of State Rex W. Tillerson heads to Alaska on Wednesday for talks on Arctic issues, he finds himself in climate policy limbo, preparing for a meeting at which global warming will be front and center yet representing an administration that i