ain': 'Questions for: ‘Prosecutors Taking Tougher Stance in Fraternity Hazing Deaths’', 'kicker': 'Article of the Day', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reading and Writing Skills (Education)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-10T08:30:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Learning', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By Caroline Crosson Gilpin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caroline', 'middlename': 'Crosson', 'lastname': 'Gilpin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c47492b-e19e-514e-861c-45f21cba5cc2', 'word_count': 377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c47492b-e19e-514e-861c-45f21cba5cc2'}, {'abstract': 'The Pulitzer Prize-winner on the Attica prison uprising, criminal-justice reform and the war on crime.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/10/magazine/heather-ann-thompson-thinks-the-justice-system-is-unfair.html', 'snippet': 'The Pulitzer Prize-winner on the Attica prison uprising, criminal-justice reform and the war on crime.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You just won a Pulitzer Prize for your history of the 1971 Attica prison uprising — and the cover-up of the atrocities that happened when the state took the prison back. How did you first become interested in civil rights issues? I grew up in Detroit in the ’70s, and everything was happening at once: The drug war was in full swing, the city of Detroit had been under black leadership for a decade, the recession had taken an incredible toll. I was growing up in the epicenter of America, a white girl in a mostly black city trying to understand all of that politically.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '62', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/magazine/14talk/14mag-14talk-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/14/magazine/14talk/14mag-14talk-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/magazine/14talk/14mag-14talk-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/magazine/14talk/14mag-14talk-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1200, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/14/magazine/14talk/14mag-14talk-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1200}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/magazine/14talk/14mag-14talk-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 512, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/magazine/14talk/14mag-14talk-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Heather Ann Thompson Thinks the Justice System Is Unfair', 'kicker': 'Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Heather Ann Thompson Thinks the Justice System Is Unfair', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thompson, Heather Ann (1963- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Blood in the Water: The Attica Prison Uprising of 1971 and Its Legacy (Book)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Attica Correctional Facility', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-10T09:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'Interview by Ana Marie Cox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Interview', 'middlename': 'Ana', 'lastname': 'Marie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67b06d97-0d1f-5b3e-abfb-d228f17efb1b', 'word_count': 697, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67b06d97-0d1f-5b3e-abfb-d228f17efb1b'}, {'abstract': 'Chatting about that heat wave isn’t banal. It’s an art form.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/10/magazine/letter-of-recommendation-talking-about-the-weather.html', 'snippet': 'Chatting about that heat wave isn’t banal. It’s an art form.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It hit a heavy, humid 90 degrees as I was walking up Sixth Avenue to get my kid from the LARPing camp we signed him up for, and my shirt clung to my skin like seaweed. Then, mercifully, a breeze picked up. And picked up some more. A woman around my age approached, pushing a toddler in a stroller. “Ah,” she said, beaming. “That wind!” She took her hands off the stroller, letting it roll, and stretched her arms out like wings. Her sleeves billowed, and she said, half to me, half to the kid, “I want to let it carry me!”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/magazine/14lor/14lor-articleLarge-v2.gif', 'height': 437, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articl