n American immigration bill 125 years ago specifically sought to exclude Chinese citizens.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2017/05/10/1892-china-us-immigration/', 'snippet': 'An American immigration bill 125 years ago specifically sought to exclude Chinese citizens.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Chinese Minister has filed in the State Department a formal protest against the Chinese Exclusion Bill. The document sets forth the following objections to the bill:— First, because it renewed the Scott Act of 1888; secondly, it deprived Chinese subjects of the right of bail in habeas corpus cases ; thirdly, it required the registration of Chinese laborers, a requirement which it was practically impossible for them to comply with, because they must all prove by white witnesses that they were lawfully entitled to be in the United States, and as the first Exclusion Act was passed in 1882, every Chinaman must produce before the Collector of Inland Revenue a white witness who knew him ten years ago, and who would swear that he was in the United States at that time.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/10/blogs/10oldmay-1892-Washington/10oldmay-1892-Washington-jumbo.png', 'height': 329, 'width': 576, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/10/blogs/10oldmay-1892-Washington/10oldmay-1892-Washington-superJumbo.png', 'height': 329, 'width': 576, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/10/blogs/10oldmay-1892-Washington/10oldmay-1892-Washington-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/201