, 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4efa14ac-e28d-5cdf-8635-96657287f2fc', 'word_count': 157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4efa14ac-e28d-5cdf-8635-96657287f2fc'}, {'abstract': 'After two international tours with “Flexn,” Reggie Gray and Peter Sellars bring “Flexn Evolution” — with social commentary — to the armory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/10/arts/dance/contortion-and-discussion-at-the-park-avenue-armory.html', 'snippet': 'After two international tours with “Flexn,” Reggie Gray and Peter Sellars bring “Flexn Evolution” — with social commentary — to the armory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2015, a group of flex dancers — expert practitioners in contorting, pausing, snapping and gliding — converged at the Park Avenue Armory for the evening-length “Flexn,” an ambitious show masterminded by Reggie Gray (who goes by Regg Roc) and Peter Sellars. Now, after two national and international tours, the collaborators return on Thursday, May 18, with “Flexn Evolution,” which promises to be more intimate, but just as virtuosic, featuring a series of choreographed and improvisational pieces inspired in part by the need for social change.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/arts/14GUIDE8/14GUIDE8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/14/arts/14GUIDE8/14GUIDE8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/arts/14GUIDE8/14GUIDE8-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/arts/14GUIDE8/14GUIDE8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/14/arts/14GUIDE8/14GUIDE8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/arts/14GUIDE8/14GUIDE8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/arts/14GUIDE8/14GUIDE8-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1354, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Contortion and Discussion at the Park Avenue Armory', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dance; The Revolution Will Be Flexed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Park Avenue Armory (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gray, Reggie (Regg Roc)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sellars, Peter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-10T15:57:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/089356dc-11d1-5b16-ac47-99790c8aa860', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/089356dc-11d1-5b16-ac47-99790c8aa860'}, {'abstract': 'Acorn streams a three-part adaptation of Evelyn Waugh’s first novel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/10/arts/television/decline-and-fall-series