 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/58740a74-8807-573f-9b37-5558585d6e72', 'word_count': 892, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58740a74-8807-573f-9b37-5558585d6e72'}, {'abstract': 'The Colombia singing star’s ‘Mis Planes Son Amarte’ follows in the mold of Beyoncé’s ‘Lemonade,’ stringing its 12 songs together in a narrative.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/10/arts/music/juanes-mis-planes-son-amarte-latin-visual-album.html', 'snippet': 'The Colombia singing star’s ‘Mis Planes Son Amarte’ follows in the mold of Beyoncé’s ‘Lemonade,’ stringing its 12 songs together in a narrative.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Colombian songwriter Juanes, a superstar across Latin America, could easily have released his new album, “Mis Planes Son Amarte” (“My Plans Are to Love You”), on its own terms: as a set of a dozen gleaming, tuneful, good-natured songs about love, featuring his amiable voice and his strategically syncopated guitars. Instead, he added another layer of ambition.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/11/arts/11JUANES1/11JUANES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/11/arts/11JUANES1/11JUANES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/11/arts/11JUANES1/11JUANES1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/11/arts/11JUANES1/11JUANES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'imag