 '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/22b2cd76-a68d-5ba7-98a1-88ee9bee962a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/22b2cd76-a68d-5ba7-98a1-88ee9bee962a'}, {'abstract': 'The man had suffered two strokes and was actively trying to prevent more. So why was he slurring his words and his face drooping?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/11/magazine/he-was-on-blood-thinners-and-supplements-could-he-still-have-had-a-stroke.html', 'snippet': 'The man had suffered two strokes and was actively trying to prevent more. So why was he slurring his words and his face drooping?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The woman was surprised to find her 69-year-old partner still in bed after she got home from church. He was usually an early riser — up and dressed by 7:30 every morning, even after he retired, even after two strokes, even after a heart attack. He just needed a little more sleep, he mumbled when she tried to rouse him. But she was worried. He was slurring his words and his face didn’t look right — it seemed strangely lopsided.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/magazine/14diagnosis1/14diagnosis1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 540, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/14/magazine/14diagnosis1/14diagnosis1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 540}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/magazine/14diagnosis1/14diagnosis1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 922, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/magazine/14diagnosis1/14diagnosis1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1250, 'width': 1389, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/magazine/14diagnosis1/14diagnosis1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/14/magazine/14diagnosis1/14diagnosis1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/magazine/14diagnosis1/14diagnosis1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'He Was on Blood Thinners and Supplements. Could He Still Have Had a Stroke?', 'kicker': 'Diagnosis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'He Was on Blood Thinners and Supplements. Could He Still Have Had a Stroke?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stroke', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Turmeric (Spice)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emergency Medical Treatment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-11T09:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Sanders, M.d', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sanders', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3cca7704-28f5-5089-ad96-445b888f138a', 'word_count': 1323, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3cca7704-28f5-5089-ad96-445b888f138a'}, {'abstract': 'The film “Get Out” is the latest horror blockbuster in an eight-year run of lean, inventive films from the Hollywood producer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/11/magazine/the-scarily-profitable-hits-of-jason-blum.html', 'snippet': 'The film “Get Out” is the latest horror blockbuster in an eight-year run of lean, inventive films from the Hollywood producer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One evening in March, Jason Blum, the 48-year-old chief executive of Blumhouse Productions, arrived late to the Bel Air mansion where he was scheduled to speak to a gathering of wealthy supporters of the Sundance Institute. He was quickly ushered into a large den, where deep couches and chairs were packed with graying donors, and glass bowls in the shape of popcorn bags were filled with king-size Butterfingers. Another speaker, the director Dee Rees, had already begun her talk. Blum is tall, square-jawed and near movie-star handsome and has made a habit of turning cheap horror movies — most recently “Get Out,” the directorial debut from the sketch comic Jordan Peele — into engines of often record-breaking profits. Blum listened intently as Rees described the hard location work on her third film, “Mudbound,” a complex period drama about racial conflict in the postwar Mississippi Delta that received a standing ovation when it had its premiere at Sundance in January. Rees finished and returned to her seat.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '44', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/magazine/14blumehouse1/14blumehouse1-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 842, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/14/magazine/14blumehouse1/14blumehouse1-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 842}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/magazine/14blumehouse1/14blumehouse1-jumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 730, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/magazine/14blumehouse1/14blumehouse1-superJumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1460, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/magazine/14blumehouse1/14blumehouse1-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/14/magazine/14blumehouse1/14blumehouse1-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/magazine/14blumehouse1/14blumehouse1-thumbLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Scarily Profitable Hits of Jason Blum', 'kicker': 'Feature', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cheap Thrills', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blum, Jason', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peele, Jordan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rees, Dee', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hawke, Ethan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Get Out (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-11T09:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ryan Bradley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ryan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bradley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 