ns for Restoring Myanmar’s Temples', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'vis-photo', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earthquakes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monuments and Memorials (Structures)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bagan (Myanmar)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monasteries and Monks', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-11T09:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Ives', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ives', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66cb5c0f-709c-5bc7-951f-e9463a74b7be', 'word_count': 1123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66cb5c0f-709c-5bc7-951f-e9463a74b7be'}, {'abstract': 'Some of the most beautiful tulips ever grown result from a virus that makes the flowers wilt early, and for that reason they are illegal in some places.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/11/science/broken-tulips.html', 'snippet': 'Some of the most beautiful tulips ever grown result from a virus that makes the flowers wilt early, and for that reason they are illegal in some places.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are 150 species of tulips, half of them wild, and thousands of varieties. They’re categorized in 15 groups, defined by characteristics like their size, bloom time, petal shape and color. During the renowned Dutch tulip festival called Keukenhof, from March to late May each year, you might get to see many of them, planted by the thousands like colorful blankets strewn across fields.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/16/science/16OBSTULIPSSUB/11TULIPS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 833, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/16/science/16OBSTULIPSSUB/11TULIPS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 833}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/16/science/16OBSTULIPSSUB/11TULIPS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 738, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/16/science/16OBSTULIPSSUB/11TULIPS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1475, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/16/science/16OBSTULIPSSUB/11TULIPS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/16/science/16OBSTULIPSSUB/11TULIPS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/16/science/16OBSTULIPSSUB/11TULIPS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Broken Tulips: ‘That Last Gasp of Beauty Before Death’', 'kicker': 'Trilobites', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Broken Blooms: A Blaze of Beauty,But It Leads to Death', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flowers and Plants', 'rank': 1, 'major':