: 798, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3e5e229-4830-5c76-8148-4fa2a317208f'}, {'abstract': 'Our critics debate a varied, and divisive, Broadway season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/11/theater/just-how-great-was-that-comet-our-critics-debate-the-broadway-season.html', 'snippet': 'Our critics debate a varied, and divisive, Broadway season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years, Ben Brantley and Jesse Green covered the same shows from different sides of the aisle, Mr. Brantley for The New York Times and Mr. Green for New York magazine. As of this month, Mr. Green has joined Mr. Brantley as co-chief theater critic for The Times. The announcement of the Tony Award nominations, with the ceremony on June 11, provides a perfect time for them to reflect on their respective experiences of a fascinatingly eclectic season, in a conversation with Scott Heller, the theater editor for The Times. Spoiler alert: disagreements ahead.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/arts/14CONVO3/14CONVO3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 362, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/14/arts/14CONVO3/14CONVO3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 362}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/arts/14CONVO3/14CONVO3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 617, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/arts/14CONVO3/14CONVO3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1235, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/arts/14CONVO3/14CONVO3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/14/arts/14CONVO3/14CONVO3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/arts/14CONVO3/14CONVO3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Just How Great Was That ‘Comet’? Our Critics Debate the Broadway Season', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Just How Great Was That ‘Comet’?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tony Awards (Theater Awards)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-11T14:00:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley and Jesse Green', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Green', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e23c94ea-e040-5384-97da-10c7437f3da6', 'word_count': 2610, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e23c94ea-e040-5384-97da-10c7437f3da6'}, {'abstract': 'The map will be sold on June 25 at Van Eaton Galleries in Sherman Oaks, Calif., and could fetch between $750,000 and $1 million.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/11/movies/walt-disney-hand-drawn-map-of-disneyland-is-headed-to-auction.html', 'snippet': 'The map will be sold on June 25 at Van Eaton Galleries in Sherman Oaks, Calif., and could fetch between $750,000 and $1 million.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the most important drawings in Disney history — which is saying something, considering it all started with doodles of a mouse — is headed to auction on June 25 at Van Eaton Galleries in Sherman Oaks, Calif. The item is a hand-colored and inked copy of an original map (with minor embellishments) that Walt Disney and a friend, Herb Ryman, created over one rushed weekend in September 1953 as part of a frantic effort to secure funding to build Disneyland.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/11/arts/12map1/12map1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 357, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/11/arts/12map1/12map1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 357}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/11/arts/12map1/12map1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 609, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/11/arts/12map1/12map1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1219, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/11/arts/12map1/12map1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/11/arts/12map1/12map1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/11/arts/12map1/12map1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Disneyland Map Is Headed to Auction', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Disneyland Map, By Disney, to Auction', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Disneyland (Anaheim, Calif)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Van Eaton Galleries (Sherman Oaks, Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Disney, Walt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryman, Herb (1910-89)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AMUSEMENT AND THEME PARKS', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-11T14:22:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72385c87-67cc-50a8-8df6-367c54f4a1a3', 'word_count': 334, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72385c87-67cc-50a8-8df6-367c54f4a1a3'}, {'abstract': 'The university released the earliest known recording of Kennedy this week, from an English class he was taking when he was 20.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/11/us/harvard-kennedy-audio.html', 'snippet': 'The university released the earliest known recording of Kennedy this week, from an English class he was taking when he was 20.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The forceful voice of the 20-year-old Harvard student punches through the crackling audio, his thick Boston accent coming to life. He is only a sophomore, but his distinct speaking style is already clear, even before he finishes the first line: “My name is John F. Kennedy.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': N