lanka-review-sri-lankan-restaurant.html', 'snippet': 'Sri Lankan restaurants are rare in New York. This one serves pizza, but the real draws are traditional specialties like the pancakes known as hoppers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'First come crackly doughnuts with rugged coppery shells, holes nearly caved in and curry leaves peeking through. They taste of salt and earth, the dough made from urad dal, split black lentils with creamy insides, soaked overnight and ground to a flour.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Caffé Lanka, an Outpost of Island Cooking in the Bronx', 'kicker': 'Hungry City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Outpost of Island Cooking in the Bronx', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Parkchester (Bronx, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Caffe Lanka (Bronx, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-11T16:23:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ligaya Mishan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ligaya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mishan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0dbd3e48-7a4e-59b4-a379-05dec56dc6be', 'word_count': 749, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0dbd3e48-7a4e-59b4-a379-05dec56dc6be'}, {'abstract': 'Suggested reading from critics and editors at The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/11/books/review/10-new-books-we-recommend-this-week.html', 'snippet': 'Suggested reading from critics and editors at The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two memoirs about parents feature among our selections this week: the poet Patricia Lockwood’s lively account of her father, a Catholic priest (long story), and the novelist Richard Ford’s reckoning with the lives of his father and mother, which leads him to a reckoning with himself. Lesley Nneka Arimah’s debut short-story collection walks the line between magical and psychological realism, and a cult classic Taiwanese novel from the 1990s explores the far reaches of intimacy and obsession. Two nonfiction works offer visions for America at home and abroad: Elizabeth Warren’s “This Fight Is Our Fight,” a manifesto for the middle class; and Condoleezza Rice’s “Democracy,” an argument that the United States should not abandon its global role as a promoter of freedom.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/books/review/14ed-covers/14ed-covers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/14/books/review/14ed-covers/14ed-covers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/books/review/14ed-covers/14ed-covers-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/books/review/14ed-covers/14ed-covers-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/14/books/review/14ed-covers/14ed-covers-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/books/review/14ed-covers/14ed-covers-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_na