es.com/2017/05/11/automobiles/autoreviews/video-review-a-competition-puts-suvs-through-their-paces.html', 'snippet': 'S.U.V.s can now be pumped with performance or stuffed with luxury. Auto reviewers gather each year to find the best.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s not news anymore that sport utility vehicles and crossovers are the vehicles that Americans prefer. The Northwest Automotive Press Association was onto the trend long before it was one, starting an Outdoor Activity Vehicle of the Year competition in 1994. Back then, S.U.V.s were truck-based vehicles and “crossover” was an aerobics move.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video Review: A Competition Puts S.U.V.s Through Their Paces', 'kicker': 'Driven', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Perfect S.U.V. to Get You to the Trail, or Through an Avalanche', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Reviews', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Utility Vehicles and Light Trucks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-11T20:01:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'subsection_name': 'New Cars', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Voelk', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Voelk', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db289503-ded7-5191-bbbc-f26b8464b631', 'word_count': 840, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db289503-ded7-5191-bbbc-f26b8464b631'}, {'abstract': 'A writer travels from Brooklyn to Lafayette, La., in search of an artist’s roots, upon the opening of an exhibition of at the Museum of Modern Art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/11/arts/design/for-robert-rauschenberg-no-artist-is-an-island.html', 'snippet': 'A writer travels from Brooklyn to Lafayette, La., in search of an artist’s roots, upon the opening of an exhibition of at the Museum of Modern Art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We tend to think of artists as natural loners, off in their studios, wrestling with their inner selves. But “Robert Rauschenberg: Among Friends,” which opens at the Museum of Modern Art on May 21, points us in a different direction. It situates Rauschenberg’s work amid that of two dozen fellow artists who provided an audience for one another in New York City in the ’50s and ’60s, the years of bohemia’s final flourish. Not that exchanges between artists are ever simple.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '33', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/arts/14RAUSCHENBERG1/14RAUSCHENBERG1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/14/arts/14RAUSCHENBERG1/14RAUSCHENBERG1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/arts/14RAUSCHENBERG1/14RAUSCHENBERG1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/arts/14RAUSCHENBERG1/14RAUSCHENBERG1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/arts/14RAUSCHENBERG1/14RAUSCHENBERG1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/14/arts/14RAUSCHENBERG1/14RAUSCHENBERG1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/arts/14RAUSCHENBERG1/14RAUSCHENBERG1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Robert Rauschenberg, No Artist Is an Island', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Rauschenberg, No Artist Is an Island', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of Modern Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rauschenberg, Robert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-11T20:01:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deborah Solomon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deborah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Solomon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/becf4474-d1fa-5722-b829-251530aa942b', 'word_count': 1741, 'uri': 'nyt://article/becf4474-d1fa-5722-b829-251530aa942b'}, {'abstract': 'The Federal Bureau of Investigation is shrouded in secrecy. Here are three books that offer insider knowledge.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/11/books/newsbook-fbi.html', 'snippet': 'The Federal Bureau of Investigation is shrouded in secrecy. Here are three books that offer insider knowledge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Donald Trump’s abrupt dismissal of James B. Comey as director of the Federal Bureau of Investigation on May 9 truncated what is typically a 10-year term, the length of which is meant to protect the bureau from political pressures. The implications of the move are being debated: Some have praised the decision, while others have questioned its timing — the F.B.I. is in the middle of investigating whether any Trump associates colluded with Russia during the 2016 presidential election. These books offer context by providing insight into the institution’s history, as well as an account of what it’s like to be on the inside.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/10/books/booksupdate/10newsbookfbi/10newsbookfbi-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/10/books/booksupdate/10newsbookfbi/10newsbookfbi-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/10/books/booksupdate/10newsbookfbi/10newsbookfbi-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/10/books/booksupdate/10newsbookfbi/10newsbookfbi-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1332, 'width': 2024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/10/books/booksupdate/10newsbookfbi/10newsbookfbi-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/10/books/booksupdate/10newsbookfbi/10newsbookfbi-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/10/books/booksupdate/10newsbookfbi/10newsbookfbi-th