, 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3907373-d43c-5845-bf2f-22f7683c1205', 'word_count': 796, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3907373-d43c-5845-bf2f-22f7683c1205'}, {'abstract': 'An author is promised information to help with book research, but doesn’t get a response after repeated emails. What to do?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/12/jobs/advice-when-they-wont-email-back.html', 'snippet': 'An author is promised information to help with book research, but doesn’t get a response after repeated emails. What to do?', 'lead_paragraph': 'How should I respond when my emails are not answered? Recently I met an individual in my field (art history), and we had an animated conversation about mutual professional interests for almost an hour. At the end, he offered to send me information to help my current book research. I followed up with an emailed appreciation and confirmation that he would send what he’d offered. No response. I tried again a week later — nothing.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/business/14workologist1/21workologist-illo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/14/business/14workologist1/21workologist-illo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/business/14workologist1/21workologist-illo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'cred