alue': 'Del Rizzo, Suzanne', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Crane Girl (Book)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manley, Curtis', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wang, Lin (Illustrator)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Hawk of the Castle: A Story of Medieval Falconry (Book)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Danna (Author)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ibatoulline, Bagram', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-12T16:52:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maria Russo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maria', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Russo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f5866f7-e599-59f5-991e-9c596100a045', 'word_count': 502, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f5866f7-e599-59f5-991e-9c596100a045'}, {'abstract': 'Nine new picture books take adventurous children out for a ride.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/12/books/review/new-picture-books-for-young-vehicle-lovers.html', 'snippet': 'Nine new picture books take adventurous children out for a ride.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1930, the Little Engine That Could chugged up a hill to test his metal. Since then, countless books featuring anthropomorphized vehicles have followed in his tracks. One of the latest is Anna Dewdney’s Little Excavator (Viking, $17.99; ages 2 to 5) — which is, sadly, a posthumous title from the beloved creator of the Llama Llama books, who had intended to start a new series. Dewdney excelled at pairing rhyme with heartfelt artwork to convey her character’s emotional journeys. The same skills are on display in “Little Excavator,” as the book’s determined protagonist struggles to help transform a vacant lot into a neighborhood park. Dewdney’s drawings of construction vehicles are as expressive as her llamas, and when Little Excavator beams with pride at the end of the book, the reader will feel the warmth.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/books/review/0514-BKS-Strum02/0514-BKS-Strum02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/14/books/review/0514-BKS-Strum02/0514-BKS-Strum02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/books/review/0514-BKS-Strum02/0514-BKS-Strum02-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/books/review/0514-BKS-Strum02/0514-BKS-Strum02-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 388, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/14/books/review/0514-BKS-Strum02/0514-BKS-Strum02-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 388}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/books/review/0514-BKS-Strum02/0514-BKS-Strum02-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 662, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/books/review/0514-BKS-Strum02/0514-BKS-Strum02-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1197, 'width': 1852, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Picture Books fo