'uri': 'nyt://article/2ecb1a09-7c42-59ff-9d3b-dc1f30d5603f'}, {'abstract': 'With the F.B.I. and Russia investigations in the news, museums and tours (including those at the White House) can offer history and insight.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/12/travel/where-to-go-scandals-and-spy-intrigue-fbi-russia.html', 'snippet': 'With the F.B.I. and Russia investigations in the news, museums and tours (including those at the White House) can offer history and insight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Donald J. Trump’s presidency and the events surrounding it have led to a revived interest in politically themed tourist sites and tours in the United States, according to Rob Stein, a travel adviser at the Stein Collective, a company in New York City specializing in trips inspired by politics. “Trump isn’t just a political figure,” he said. ”He’s like a controversial reality TV star, and because of him, the general public is more engaged in current politics and thrilling topics like spying and scandals.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/travel/12update/12update-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 698, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/14/travel/12update/12update-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 698}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/travel/12update/12update-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 880, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/travel/12update/12update-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1760, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': '