mmencement is for those graduating, not for people promoting their own agendas. College administrators need to realize that.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/12/opinion/why-graduation-and-controversial-speakers-dont-mix.html', 'snippet': 'Commencement is for those graduating, not for people promoting their own agendas. College administrators need to realize that.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Education Secretary Betsy DeVos delivered a commencement address this week at Bethune-Cookman University, a historically black institution in Florida, she was greeted with a predictable chorus of boos.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/12/opinion/12OnCampus/12OnCampus-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/12/opinion/12OnCampus/12OnCampus-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/12/opinion/12OnCampus/12OnCampus-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/12/opinion/12OnCampus/12OnCampus-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 434, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/12/opinion/12OnCampus/12OnCampus-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 434}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/12/opinion/12OnCampus/12OnCampus-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 741, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/12/opinion/12OnCampus/12OnCampus-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1483, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Graduation and Controversial Speakers Don’t Mix', 'kicker': 'On Campus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Commencement Speeches', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DeVos, Elizabeth (1958- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-12T21:13:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Murray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/febf30f1-8201-53f3-9f6e-1deb0be833fd', 'word_count': 554, 'uri': 'nyt://article/febf30f1-8201-53f3-9f6e-1deb0be833fd'}, {'abstract': 'A deeply personal work has been accompanied in recent concerts by reflections on mortality, the planet and the Syrian refugee crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/12/arts/music/how-brahmss-a-german-requiem-became-an-anthem-for-our-time.html', 'snippet': 'A deeply personal work has been accompanied in recent concerts by reflections on mortality, the planet and the Syrian refugee crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York concert season now drawing to a close was more or less bookended by performances of Brahms’s “A German Requiem,” intended to set the work in broader contexts. In October, Lincoln Center presented “human requiem,” featuring Simon Halsey and the Berlin Radio Choir in an immersive staging,