Self-expression through clothing was so strong at that point,” she said. “Making a mark by showing who you are was the way to get noticed.” After taking a break from street style to focus on personal projects and commercial work, she recently returned to it. “I thought for a long time that people weren’t as interested in style as they used to be,” she said,  adding that “something about the resistance has brought back what we wear as a statement now.”   ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Amy Arbus Returns to Shooting Style, This Time Focusing on Headwear', 'kicker': 'THE LOOK', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hats and Caps', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Village Voice', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ARBUS, DIANE', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Avedon, Richard', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington Square Park (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-13T10:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Arbus, Joanna Nikas and Eve Lyons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Arbus', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Joanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nikas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Eve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3eec077-70e5-55d7-aadd-18473fd16bfa', 'word_count': 968, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3eec077-70e5-