, 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/opinion/14rattner-img/14rattner-img-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/14/opinion/14rattner-img/14rattner-img-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/opinion/14rattner-img/14rattner-img-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/opinion/14rattner-img/14rattner-img-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Trump Claims to Have Saved U.S. Jobs. But How Many, Really?', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trump’s Job Creation: His Claims vs. Reality', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Exxon Mobil Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indiana', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-13T18:59:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Rattner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rattner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/40e7d7de-dca0-5da1-97cd-903148cb0e3e', 'word_count': 306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40e7d7de-dca0-5da1-97cd-903148cb0e3e'}, {'abstract': 'An arbitrary sense of “balance” isn’t good, but unbalanced coverage ought to give pause.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/13/opinion/sunday/is-it-possible-there-is-nothing-nice-to-say.html', 'snippet': 'An arbitrary sense of “balance” isn’t good, but unbalanced coverage ought to give pause.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Donald Trump is a hated figure — more hated than any political figure in America. In Washington you can just assume that any random person you talk with agrees with you about that. The only comparable person in American politics is Richard Nixon, who my mother told me was despicable when I was about 6, long before Watergate — and she was right!', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/opinion/sunday/14kinsley/14kinsley-articleLarge.gif', 'height': 443, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/14/opinion/sunday/14kinsley/14kinsley-articleLarge.gif', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 443}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/opinion/sunday/14kinsley/14kinsley-jumbo.gif', 'height': 756, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/opinion/sunday/14kinsley/14kinsley-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 815, 'width': 1092, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/opinion/sunday/14kinsley/14kinsley-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/14/opinion/sunday/14kinsley/14kinsley-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/opinion/sunday/14kinsley/14kinsley-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Is It Possible There Is Nothing Nice to Say?', 'kicker': 'Opinion | Say Something Nice About Donald Trump', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Can There Be Nothing Good to Say?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-13T19:01:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Kinsley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kinsley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/71430291-c365-59fe-905c-ed15a7d57993', 'word_count': 490, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71430291-c365-59fe-905c-ed15a7d57993'}, {'abstract': 'I am obsessed with a video game console I don’t own.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/13/opinion/the-nintendo-switch-of-my-dreams.html', 'snippet': 'I am obsessed with a video game console I don’t own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I am a 34-year-old woman who is obsessed with the Switch — Nintendo’s newest and best gaming console, which came out in March. Small problem: I’ve banned myself from getting one. Another problem: The thing is hard to get. Some 2.7 million people rushed to buy the Switch, with its hybrid controllers and portable screen, when it was released, and demand outstripped supply. Now many retailers have been out of stock for weeks, and others have marked up the precious console by hundreds of dollars.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/opinion/sunday/14stefanovic/14stefanovic-articleLarge.gif', 'height': 449, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/14/opinion/sunday/14stefanovic/14stefanovic-articleLarge.gif', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 449}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/opinion/sunday/14stefanovic/14stefanovic-jumbo.gif', 'height': 766, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/opinion/sunday/14stefanovic/14stefanovic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1311, 'width': 2016, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/opinion/sunday/14stefanovic/14stefanovic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/14/opinion/sunday/14stefanovic/14stefanovic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/opinion/sunday/14stefanovic/14stefanovic-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height':