 'My generation is spending more money than ever before on these kids. Not to mention time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/13/opinion/sunday/grandbabies-the-great-reward-for-aging.html', 'snippet': 'My generation is spending more money than ever before on these kids. Not to mention time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Happy Mother’s Day to all us grandmothers, we band of lovesick indulgers whose ability to say no seems to be disabled the day our grandbabies are born. We sneak them candy when Mom says no, we let them play on iPads, read them “Fancy Nancy” over and over … and over. We get out our wallets whenever they point to something and say, “I want dat.” Yup, that’s us. And it’s Grampa, too. Someone wise said, “If God had asked Abraham to sacrifice his grandson, he’d have said, ‘No way!’ ”', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/opinion/sunday/14stahl/14stahl-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/14/opinion/sunday/14stahl/14stahl-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/opinion/sunday/14stahl/14stahl-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/opinion/sunday/14stahl/14stahl-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/14/opinion/sunday/14stahl/14stahl-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 409}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/opinion/sunday/14stahl/14stahl-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 698, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/opinion/sunday/14stahl/14stahl-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1296, 'width': 1901, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Grandbabies: The Great Reward for Aging', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Grandbabies: The Great Reward', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grandparents', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-13T21:26:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lesley Stahl', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lesley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stahl', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/38313466-11a4-5bf4-9a66-be5716063901', 'word_count': 993, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38313466-11a4-5bf4-9a66-be5716063901'}, {'abstract': 'She freed herself of every convention but one: the fear that she would be judged a bad mother.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/13/opinion/sunday/thanks-to-mom-the-marxist-revolutionary.html', 'snippet': 'She freed herself of every convention but one: the fear that she would be judged a bad mother.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My mother hated Mother’s Day. She was a 1950s Mennonite housewife from Kansas who became a 1960s radical promoting the overthrow of patriarchy and capitalism. She saw Mother’s Day as a conspiracy between Hallmark and the flower industry, but she was always happy to take my call.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source':