 'nyt://article/9aa641db-d079-5242-8ef7-636b07dd7374'}, {'abstract': 'The conductor Leon Botstein champions a little-known Elgar oratorio in a stirring performance with the American Symphony Orchestra at Carnegie Hall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/14/arts/music/review-elgars-the-apostles-american-symphony-orchestra-leon-botstein.html', 'snippet': 'The conductor Leon Botstein champions a little-known Elgar oratorio in a stirring performance with the American Symphony Orchestra at Carnegie Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The conductor Leon Botstein has long argued that classical music is in danger of boring itself to death with endless performances of repertory staples, however great those works may be. Through the programs he has conducted over 25 years as music director of the American Symphony Orchestra, and the summer festivals he has overseen at Bard College, where he is president, Mr. Botstein has championed earlier works that, often for inexplicable reasons, have been nearly forgotten.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/15/arts/15ASO/15ASO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/15/arts/15ASO/15ASO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/15/arts/15ASO/15ASO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/15/arts/15ASO/15ASO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 842, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/15/arts/15ASO/15ASO-articleLarg