 songs of romantic angst and festering loneliness.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/14/arts/music/niia-i-robin-hannibal.html', 'snippet': 'This singer’s voice seeps into all the crevices and pockets of her album’s lush productions on songs of romantic angst and festering loneliness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Niia sings like a slow pour. On “Sideline,” one of this year’s most arresting soul songs, she begins with sauntering scatting, part jazz and part Suzanne Vega, before easing into millennial romantic angst: “Yeah I know she’s still the background on your phone.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/15/arts/15NIIA-1/15NIIA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 456, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/15/arts/15NIIA-1/15NIIA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 456}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/15/arts/15NIIA-1/15NIIA-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 778, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/15/arts/15NIIA-1/15NIIA-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1555, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/15/arts/15NIIA-1/15NIIA-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/15/arts/15NIIA-1/15NIIA-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/15/arts/15NIIA-1/15NIIA-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On Niia’s Debut Album, ‘I,’ Soul That Melts and Trip-Hop That Oozes', 'kicker': 'Album Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Smooth Soul, Angst Accents', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hannibal, Robin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pop and Rock Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bertino, Niia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'I (Album)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-14T21:27:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f52fdccd-5c71-5d38-ae4c-5810e36e8ae9', 'word_count': 547, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f52fdccd-5c71-5d38-ae4c-5810e36e8ae9'}, {'abstract': 'The focus of this HBO documentary is the killing of Dee Dee Blanchard, a case in which Ms. Blanchard’s daughter and her boyfriend became suspects.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/14/arts/television/review-the-bizarre-case-of-mommy-dead-and-dearest.html', 'snippet': 'The focus of this HBO documentary is the killing of Dee Dee Blanchard, a case in which Ms. Blanchard’s daughter and her boyfriend became suspects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some true-crime documentaries have to embellish and overstate to justify giving so much attention to a garden-variety criminal case. Not “Mommy Dead and Dearest,” which has its premiere Monday night on HBO. The strangeness of this killing speaks for itself, and the director, Erin Lee Carr, largely just lets it do so.', 