 Kobach, the Kansas secretary of state, oversees an office whose clerical and regulatory work costs the state’s taxpayers barely $5.5 million a year. But he has parlayed that modest post into a national platform for tough restrictions on voting rights and immigration, becoming both a celebrated voice within the Republican Party and a regular target of lawsuits by civil rights advocates.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/15/us/15kobach/15kobach-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/15/us/15kobach/15kobach-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/15/us/15kobach/15kobach-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/15/us/15kobach/15kobach-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/15/us/15kobach/15kobach-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/15/us/15kobach/15kobach-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/15/us/15kobach/15kobach-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Advocate for Tough Voting Rules to Steer Trump’s Elections Commission', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A ‘Passionate’ Seeker of Voter Fraud in Kansas Gets a National Soapbox', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kobach, Kris W', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kansas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigration', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-14T23:18:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Wines and Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b060796-63fe-549f-855d-df39ab8084a5', 'word_count': 1436, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b060796-63fe-549f-855d-df39ab8084a5'}, {'abstract': 'The Mets led, 7-1, after five innings, but that was not enough for Jacob deGrom and a string of relievers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/14/sports/baseball/new-york-mets-collapse-milwaukee-brewers-jacob-degrom.html', 'snippet': 'The Mets led, 7-1, after five innings, but that was not enough for Jacob deGrom and a string of relievers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MILWAUKEE — The reasons the Mets could have won on Sunday were many: Their offense produced nine runs on 15 hits; Jacob deGrom, one of their best able-bodied starters, had a 7-1 lead midway through the game; and three of the four relievers they used had been off the three previous days.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/15/sports/15METS1/15METS1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/15/sports/15METS1/15METS1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/15/sports/15METS1/15METS1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/15/sports/15METS1/15METS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/15/sports/15METS1/15METS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/15/sports/15METS1/15METS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/15/sports/15METS1/15METS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mets Build a Six-Run Lead, Then Lose by Two', 'kicker': 'Brewers 11, Mets 9', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mets’ Slide Drags On As a Lead Vanishes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Milwaukee Brewers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'deGrom, Jacob', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Milwaukee (Wis)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-14T23:24:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Wagner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wagner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f654bdc6-36e4-52d6-af34-70299a17b0ea', 'word_count': 856, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f654bdc6-36e4-52d6-af34-70299a17b0ea'}, {'abstract': 'Rogue soldiers have staged a mutiny over back pay and better living conditions in Bouaké, setting up a tense standoff with the government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/14/world/africa/ivory-coast-military-mutiny-bouake.html', 'snippet': 'Rogue soldiers have staged a mutiny over back pay and better living conditions in Bouaké, setting up a tense standoff with the government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ABIDJAN, Ivory Coast — The Ivory Coast government sent a convoy of elite forces to the city of Bouaké on Sunday in an effort to quell a three-day military mutiny over pay that has already left one former rebel dead and five civilians wounded.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/15/world/15ivory/15ivory-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 412, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/15/world/15ivory/15ivory-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 412}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/15/world/15ivory/15ivory-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 704, '