n Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5df5651-290d-58d4-9c84-bebb2456a660', 'word_count': 774, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5df5651-290d-58d4-9c84-bebb2456a660'}, {'abstract': 'Just because the end might be nigh doesn’t mean it’s a good idea to board an Australian sex cult cruise. Even if you’re man of the cloth like Matt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/14/arts/television/the-leftovers-recap-its-a-matt-matt-matt-matt-world.html', 'snippet': 'Just because the end might be nigh doesn’t mean it’s a good idea to board an Australian sex cult cruise. Even if you’re man of the cloth like Matt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The trials of Job were just a pop quiz in comparison to how much God has tested the Mapleton pastor Matt Jamison through three seasons of “The Leftovers.” In the third episode of Season 1, he won and lost a fortune during a few furious days of gambling and crusading. In the fifth episode of Season 2, he found out his comatose wife, Mary, was pregnant, just before the two of them were locked out of Jarden with the rabble at the town’s gates. There’s a pattern to these Matt episodes. He ventures outside of his everyday bubble and experiences something miraculous ... right before he gets the wind knocked out of him.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/14/arts/television/14leftovers/14leftovers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/14/arts/television/14leftovers/14leftovers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url':