uri': 'nyt://article/dba21c7c-5f4e-5314-bb50-aa75fbee3076'}, {'abstract': 'Nicolas Ghesquière’s 2018 resort collection mixed his love of the country’s aesthetic with its girl-gang films of the 1970s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/15/fashion/louis-vuitton-nicolas-ghesquiere-cruise-2018.html', 'snippet': 'Nicolas Ghesquière’s 2018 resort collection mixed his love of the country’s aesthetic with its girl-gang films of the 1970s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cellphone service was bad in the more remote valleys outside Kyoto, Japan, so there was some question as to when Nicolas Ghesquière, the artistic director of Louis Vuitton, would call. He was meant to be dialing me, at home in New York, to discuss his cruise collection, which he showed at the Miho Museum, about an hour’s drive east of Kyoto, on Sunday. The museum, designed by I. M. Pei to display the antiquities collection of Mihoko Koyama, is in a far-flung location, tricky to get to and, even among the well-traveled and well-informed, fairly obscure.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/16/fashion/15notebook-1/15notebook-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/16/fashion/15notebook-1/15notebook-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/16/fashion/15notebook-1/15notebook-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/16/fashion/15notebook-1/15notebook-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017