e for hungry shoppers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/15/dining/food-canal-street-market.html', 'snippet': 'The large market in Chinatown features ramen, dumplings, rice bowls and more for hungry shoppers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When it opened in December, the Canal Street Market offered plenty of shopping options, but the planned food hall was not ready. Now a dozen stands, many selling Asian foods, are operating in the stately building. There’s Uma Temakeria for hand-rolled sushi, Nom Wah Kuai for dumplings and rice bowls, Oppa for Korean barbecue items, Ilili Box for Middle Eastern, Boba Guys for milk teas, and Kuro-Obi by Ippudo New York for ramen. Billy’s Bakery will have a cart in a few days: Canal Street Market Food Hall, 265 Canal Street (Broadway), 646-694-1655, canalstreet.market.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/17/dining/17Burnermarket/17Burnermarket-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/17/dining/17Burnermarket/17Burnermarket-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/17/dining/17Burnermarket/17Burnermarket-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/17/dining/17Burnermarket/17Burnermarket-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 381, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/17/dining/17Burnermarket/17Burnermarket-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 381}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'capt