96-9bb7-8b2b21d81dec'}, {'abstract': 'Jonathan Blum, a lawyer and soy sauce connoisseur, is importing Shiso handcrafted soy sauces from Japan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/15/dining/shiso-soy-sauce-japan.html', 'snippet': 'Jonathan Blum, a lawyer and soy sauce connoisseur, is importing Shiso handcrafted soy sauces from Japan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Within these elegant bottles are two artisanal soy sauces: Koikuchi is a traditional style delivering a sharp edge, and Marudai, made from whole soy beans, is richer, rounder and more complex. Shiso soy sauces are brewed in the Shimane Prefecture in southwestern Japan by a family that has been in the business for six generations. Both contain wheat, but they have no additives or preservatives and ferment longer than supermarket brands. Jonathan Blum, a lawyer, imports them. He even describes sushi etiquette on his company’s website: Shiso Koikuchi, $16, Marudai, $18 (3.4 ounces each), $30 for both, shisosoy.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/17/dining/17Burnersauce/Burnersauce-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/17/dining/17Burnersauce/Burnersauce-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/17/dining/17Burnersauce/Burnersauce-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/17/dining/17Burnersauce/Burnersauce-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 777, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05