astrophe set off an unexpected shortage of iodine, leaving children in faraway countries vulnerable to cognitive deficits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The tsunami and nuclear disaster in Fukushima, Japan, now threatens the developing brains of children in Cambodia — but not for reasons that were ever expected.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/16/science/16SCI-GLOBAL2/16SCI-GLOBAL2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 378, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/16/science/16SCI-GLOBAL2/16SCI-GLOBAL2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 378}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/16/science/16SCI-GLOBAL2/16SCI-GLOBAL2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 646, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/16/science/16SCI-GLOBAL2/16SCI-GLOBAL2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1291, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/16/science/16SCI-GLOBAL2/16SCI-GLOBAL2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/16/science/16SCI-GLOBAL2/16SCI-GLOBAL2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/16/science/16SCI-GLOBAL2/16SCI-GLOBAL2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How a Tsunami in Japan Endangered Children in Cambodia', 'kicker': 'Global Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Cure for Cambodia’s Children', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iodine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japan Earthquake and Tsunami (2011)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Thyroid Gland', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cambodia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-15T16:13:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Donald G. McNeil Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Donald', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'McNeil', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29b92ff2-16db-54e2-be35-2d2b2186fdb5', 'word_count': 841, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29b92ff2-16db-54e2-be35-2d2b2186fdb5'}, {'abstract': 'At 375° Fries on the Lower East Side, potatoes are steamed, par-cooked and then fried to order for that crispy-outside, creamy-inside ideal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/15/dining/375-fries-french-fry-lower-east-side.html', 'snippet': 'At 375° Fries on the Lower East Side, potatoes are steamed, par-cooked and then fried to order for that crispy-outside, creamy-inside ideal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few years ago, French fry shops were opening faster than you could say “ketchup or mayo?” Then the trend subsided, and most disappeared. But they may be coming back. First came Bar à Frites at Le District, and now there is 375° Fries on the Lower East Side, where the potatoes are cooked three times, not the usual two. They’re steamed, then lightly par-cooked, frozen and finally fried to order in hot oil at 375 degrees, hence the name. The fries emerge properly crisp, well burnished and with a creamy interior. Extravagant nacho, poutine, okonomiyaki and other toppings turn them into a more substantial snack. The shop has Keith Haring-style graffiti and counter seating: 375° Fries, 124 Ludlow Street (Rivington Street), 646-682-7578, 375fries.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/17/dining/17Burner-fry/17Burner-fry-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/17/dining/17Burner-fry/17Burner-fry-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/17/dining/17Burner-fry/17Burner-fry-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/17/dining/17Burner-fry/17Burner-fry-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/17/dining/17Burner-fry/17Burner-fry-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/17/dining/17Burner-fry/17Burner-fry-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/17/dining/17Burner-fry/17Burner-fry-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Cooking Fries, New Shop Says Three Times