, Andrej', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zaoralek, Lubomir', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sobotka, Bohuslav', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Czech Republic', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-15T17:13:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hana de Goeij', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de Goeij', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fecfd7bb-afb0-545b-9d53-69524e62f922', 'word_count': 630, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fecfd7bb-afb0-545b-9d53-69524e62f922'}, {'abstract': 'The series is based on the author and filmmaker Chris Kraus’s autobiographical, experimental first novel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/15/watching/i-love-dick-review-roundup-good-articles.html', 'snippet': 'The series is based on the author and filmmaker Chris Kraus’s autobiographical, experimental first novel.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I Love Dick,” the new Amazon comedy created with Jill Soloway, the Emmy-winning creator of “Transparent,” comes with a back story that spans two decades. The series is based on the author and filmmaker Chris Kraus’s autobiographical, experimental first novel of the same name, which has become a feminist cult classic since its publication in 1997. Both versions follow Chris (Kathryn Hahn), a failing filmmaker, as she falls suddenly and completely in love with a mysterious intellectual named Dick (a character inspired, in the book, by the media theorist Dick Hebdige and played, on the show, by Kevin Bacon). In a perverse twist, she is egged on in her obsession by her husband, Dick’s colleague Sylvère (Griffin Dunne), who is based on Kraus’s real-life ex, Sylvère Lotringer. Structured as a series of letters to Dick, the book reads more like an essay on love, art and philosophy than like a traditional novel — which makes it a pretty unlikely candidate for adaptation as a sitcom.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/12/arts/I-Love-Dick-Watching/I-Love-Dick-Watching-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/12/arts/I-Love-Dick-Watching/I-Love-Dick-Watching-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/12/arts/I-Love-Dick-Watching/I-Love-Dick-Watching-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/12/arts/I-Love-Dick-Watching/I-Love-Dick-Watching-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 415, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/12/arts/I-Love-Dick-Watching/I-Love-Dick-Watching-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 415}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/12/arts/I-Love-Dick-Watching/I-Love-Dick-Watching-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 708, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/12/arts/I-Love-Dick-Watching/I-Love-Dick-Watching-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1416, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What to Read Before You Watch Jill Soloway’s New Show ‘I Love Dick’', 'kicker': 'Chatter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2017-05-15T17:13:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Watching', 'section_name': 'Watching', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Berman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc9a6e91-a5d4-5848-a47f-77d0dfe67b41', 'word_count': 886, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc9a6e91-a5d4-5848-a47f-77d0dfe67b41'}, {'abstract': 'The actor had lent his burly frame and Texas drawl to TV and films since the 1970s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/15/arts/powers-boothe-dead.html', 'snippet': 'The actor had lent his burly frame and Texas drawl to TV and films since the 1970s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Powers Boothe, an actor best known for playing dark characters on television shows like “Deadwood” and in movies like “Sin City,” died on Sunday at his home in Los Angeles. He was 68.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/16/obituaries/16xp-boothe/16xp-boothe-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/16/obituaries/16xp-boothe/16xp-boothe-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/16/obituaries/16xp-boothe/16xp-boothe-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/16/obituaries/16xp-boothe/16xp-boothe-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'wid