ance.”) Curios fill the walls and shelves: There’s the Florentine tabernacle, “dragged back from Tuscany,” and Saint Valentine’s tooth, nestled in a reliquary that Krascella found in Sicily. Iranian pomegranates, dried and hand-painted, sit alongside a selection of scarabs from Luxor, Egypt. “I travel a lot,” he says. “Can you tell?”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/15/t-magazine/fashion/jed-slide-HD41/jed-slide-HD41-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/15/t-magazine/fashion/jed-slide-HD41/jed-slide-HD41-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/15/t-magazine/fashion/jed-slide-HD41/jed-slide-HD41-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/15/t-magazine/fashion/jed-slide-HD41/jed-slide-HD41-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1358, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/15/t-magazine/fashion/jed-slide-HD41/jed-slide-HD41-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/15/t-magazine/fashion/jed-slide-HD41/jed-slide-HD41-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/15/t-magazine/fashion/jed-slide-HD41/jed-slide-HD41-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 