ons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-17T17:29:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maggie Haberman and Glenn Thrush', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maggie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thrush', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1fb4089a-1f66-5864-90eb-c948a5fa0c04', 'word_count': 821, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1fb4089a-1f66-5864-90eb-c948a5fa0c04'}, {'abstract': 'Upheaval at the White House and a growing list of matters for Congress to address have made the prospect even of tax cuts likely to be pushed into the next year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/17/us/politics/tax-code-republicans-ryan-mcconnell.html', 'snippet': 'Upheaval at the White House and a growing list of matters for Congress to address have made the prospect even of tax cuts likely to be pushed into the next year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Only two months ago, Republicans in Congress and President Trump’s top economic advisers were confidently predicting that a sweeping rewrite of the tax code would be in hand by summer’s end.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/18/us/18taxes/18taxes-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/18/us/18taxes/18taxes-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/