, 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/eda6697e-f945-55d9-8295-86359f173cb4', 'word_count': 220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eda6697e-f945-55d9-8295-86359f173cb4'}, {'abstract': 'Celebrate the revival with sweet ’50-ish dresses, saddle shoes, Americana jeans and a tee (taken from the boys).', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/17/fashion/twin-peaks-shopping-style.html', 'snippet': 'Celebrate the revival with sweet ’50-ish dresses, saddle shoes, Americana jeans and a tee (taken from the boys).', 'lead_paragraph': 'After two and a half decades, the fog over the town of Twin Peaks may finally be lifting: The cult series, which ended on a cliffhanger in 1991, is set to return on Sunday. The new series, “Twin Peaks:\xa0The Return,” on Showtime, picks up with Special Agent Dale Cooper and the gang 25-plus years after the mysterious death of Laura Palmer. With the founding creators David Lynch and Mark Frost and much of the\xa0original cast\xa0on board, we can expect a trippy and addictive ride. The visuals, of course, will provide fertile ground for inspiration, particularly the fashion, which will come from Nancy Steiner, whose portfolio includes “The Virgin Suicides” and “Lost in Translation.” Here, looks inspired by the show’s most seminal imagery to get you in the spirit for the premiere.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/18/fashion/18BROWSE1234combo/18BROWSE1234combo-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 215, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/18/fashion/18BROWSE1234combo/18BROWSE1234combo-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 215}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/18/fashion/18BROWSE1234combo/18BROWSE1234combo-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 368, 'width': 1024, 's