nt landfills, stoking our most primal browsing habits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/17/arts/lost-in-the-digital-swamp-link-by-link.html', 'snippet': 'Companies occupy real estate at the margins of websites and fill them with links to content landfills, stoking our most primal browsing habits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was on my phone, reading an article from a respectable news outlet, when I came across an ad tempting me toward a seedier corner of the web. It featured a photograph of an anonymous woman leaning over the bathroom sink, her head cut out of the frame, backside front and center, iPhone gleaming on the counter nearby. “Husband Divorced His Wife After Looking Closer at This Photo,” the headline read.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/18/arts/18WEBTAXONOMYJP/18WEBTAXONOMYJP-jumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 231, 'width': 560, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/18/arts/18WEBTAXONOMYJP/18WEBTAXONOMYJP-superJumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 231, 'width': 560, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/18/arts/18WEBTAXONOMYJP/18WEBTAXONOMYJP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/18/arts/18WEBTAXONOMYJP/18WEBTAXONOMYJP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lost in the Digital Swamp, Link by Link', 'kicker': "Critic's Notebook", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Getting Lost  In a Swamp, Link by Link', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Outbrain Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taboola Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-17T21:11:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amanda Hess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d65a6861-0cf0-5485-97c6-e38dbebd6833', 'word_count': 1346, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d65a6861-0cf0-5485-97c6-e38dbebd6833'}, {'abstract': 'There’s a renovation to celebrate at Saks, a block party in SoHo and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/17/fashion/where-to-shop-for-summer-this-weekend.html', 'snippet': 'There’s a renovation to celebrate at Saks, a block party in SoHo and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Thursday at 7 p.m., stop by the Collective, the trend-merchandized shopping experience on the newly renovated fifth floor of Saks Fifth Avenue’s New York flagship. You can pick up a Public School long lace dress ($895) or a Tanya Taylor embroidered military jacket ($695) and meet the designers. Ten percent of proceeds from sales through Saturday will be donated to the NewYork-Presbyterian Phyllis and David Komansky Center for Children’s Health.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/18/fashion/18scout2/18scout2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 415, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/18/fashion/18scout2/18scout2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 415}}, {'