he arson arrest after a blaze burned to the ground the landmark building on the Lower East Side that formerly housed Beth Hamedrash Hagodol.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/17/nyregion/teenager-set-manhattan-synagogue-ablaze-police-say.html', 'snippet': 'The police made the arson arrest after a blaze burned to the ground the landmark building on the Lower East Side that formerly housed Beth Hamedrash Hagodol.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For eight generations in the life of a city that changed constantly around them, the twin towers on Norfolk Street beckoned the faithful on Manhattan’s Lower East Side: first, Baptists, whose congregation was the forerunner of the Riverside Church; then Methodists; and then, for 122 years, Orthodox Jews from Eastern Europe, who called the synagogue Beth Hamedrash Hagodol — the Great House of Study.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/18/nyregion/18SYNAGOGUE/18SYNAGOGUE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/18/nyregion/18SYNAGOGUE/18SYNAGOGUE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/18/nyregion/18SYNAGOGUE/18SYNAGOGUE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/18/nyregion/18SYNAGOGUE/18SYNAGOGUE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/18/nyregion/18SYNAGOGUE/18SYNAGOGUE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'wid