'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gubar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1329e4e1-cdec-5542-bf65-95942b6487bd', 'word_count': 842, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1329e4e1-cdec-5542-bf65-95942b6487bd'}, {'abstract': 'The Pulitzer Prize-winning television critic for The New Yorker joins Jenna Wortham and Wesley Morris to discuss how shows such as “Veep,” “The Handmaid’s Tale” and “The Leftovers” speak to our new political reality.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/18/podcasts/what-tv-should-we-watch-in-the-trump-era-emily-nussbaum-has-some-ideas.html', 'snippet': 'The Pulitzer Prize-winning television critic for The New Yorker joins Jenna Wortham and Wesley Morris to discuss how shows such as “Veep,” “The Handmaid’s Tale” and “The Leftovers” speak to our new political reality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Did anyone else experience déjà vu when James Comey was fired last week? We thought it reminded us of something, but we couldn’t put our finger on it — until we spent some time in the archives of YouTube, watching old clips of “Celebrity Apprentice.” It turns out that hints of Donald Trump’s style of governance are right there in the boardroom scenes: not just his penchant for sudden dismissals, but also how much he relishes performing the role of a powerful person. We invited Emily Nussbaum, the Pulitzer Prize-winning television critic for The New Yorker to talk with us about Trump’s obsession with TV and what shows we should consider watching in the wake of Trump. We take a look at the rise of fictional television shows that seem to speak to our new political reality — shows like “Veep,” “The Handmaid’s Tale” and “The Leftovers.” Those last two are set in dystopian versions of the future, where abnormal, unsettling events begin to seem ordinary, and they prompted us to ask a question: When we turn to art to explain to us a world that feels increasingly unreal, what can it tell us?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/18/magazine/18mag-still-processing-1/18mag-still-processing-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/18/magazine/18mag-still-processing-1/18mag-still-processing-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/18/magazine/18mag-still-processing-1/18mag-still-processing-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/18/magazine/18mag-still-processing-1/18mag-still-processing-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/18/magazine/18mag-still-processing-1/18mag-still-processing-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/18/magazine/18mag-still-processing-1/18mag-still-processing-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/18/magazine/18mag-still-processing-1/18mag-still-processing-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What TV Should We Watch in the Trump Era? Emily Nussbaum Has Some Ideas.', 'kicker': 'Still Processing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Podcasts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reality Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Celebrity Apprentice (TV Program)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Leftovers (TV Program)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Veep (TV Program)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-18T10:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Podcasts', 'section_name': 'Podcasts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Wesley Morris and Jenna Wortham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Wesley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jenna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wortham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8fa4d2e-d47a-5df8-a1c3-9220f9b9b762', 'word_count': 493, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8fa4d2e-d47a-5df8-a1c3-9220f9b9b762'}, {'abstract': 'There’s been a year’s worth of headlines in just a week. It’s been exasperating for some, exhausting for many.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/18/us/trying-not-to-drown-in-a-flood-of-trump-news.html', 'snippet': 'There’s been a year’s worth of headlines in just a week. It’s been exasperating for some, exhausting for many.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What a year the last few days have been, huh?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/17/us/00xp-social/00xp-social-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy':