f-recommendation-mr-met.html', 'snippet': 'A smiling, baseball-headed constant in a world of constant change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not long ago, The New York Post heralded the arrival of a new king of the city. There on the front page, beneath a jaunty crown, was the grinning visage of Mr. Met. For the first time since people started monitoring such things, the Mets — the perennial punch line, the professional underdogs — had eclipsed the Yankees in popularity among New York City baseball fans. Lovers of the National League franchise, who’ve always cherished a vague sense of moral superiority, felt briefly vindicated. I couldn’t help noticing that it was Mr. Met — and not the actual players — who was coronated.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/21/magazine/21lor/21mag-21lor-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 415, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/21/magazine/21lor/21mag-21lor-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 415}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/21/magazine/21lor/21mag-21lor-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 709, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/21/magazine/21lor/21mag-21lor-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1417, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/21/magazine/21lor/21mag-21lor-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/21/magazine/21lor/21mag-2