-6f85-52ec-affe-dd3a8365f993'}, {'abstract': 'The plan suggested by Per-Erik Muskos, a politician in the northern town of Overtornea, had drawn a mixture of astonishment, glee and derision.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/18/world/europe/sweden-sex-leave-town.html', 'snippet': 'The plan suggested by Per-Erik Muskos, a politician in the northern town of Overtornea, had drawn a mixture of astonishment, glee and derision.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When a politician in a small town in northern Sweden recently suggested that it subsidize one-hour sex breaks for local employees, Swedes — and people around the world — reacted with a mixture of astonishment, glee and derision.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Swedish Town Rejects Proposal to Grant Sex Leave to Workers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Swedish Town Rejects Plan to Let Workers Take a Break for Sex', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Working Hours', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Work-Life Balance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sweden', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-18T14:45:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Bilefsky and Christina Anderson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilefsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Christina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Anderson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7a32eae-235f-5342-ac5c-df1a026d09d8', 'word_count': 592, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7a32eae-235f-5342-ac5c-df1a026d09d8'}, {'abstract': 'Anecdotal ledes have bedeviled Times executives at least since 1980. But they are easier to deplore than to cull.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/18/insider/if-you-have-an-hour-or-two-to-spare-ive-got-a-story.html', 'snippet': 'Anecdotal ledes have bedeviled Times executives at least since 1980. But they are easier to deplore than to cull.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Still somewhat spry at 65 and looking — or so he believed — like a bespectacled, balding Jimmy Olsen in one of those narrow bow ties he favored, David W. Dunlap settled into a window cubicle overlooking an unprepossessing stretch of West 41st Street, took three or four sips of his black French Roast coffee, inhaled shallowly and held that breath. Then he opened his email.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/18/insider/18insider-anecdote/18insider-anecdote-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/18/insider/18insider-anecdote/18insider-anecdote-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/18/insider/18insider-anecdote/18insider-anecdote-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/18/insider/18insider-anecdote/18insider-anecdote-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 821, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/18/insider/18insider-anecdote/18insider-anecdote-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 821}}, {'rank': 0,