ons', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-18T19:14:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Schmitt and Anne Barnard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8aa14daa-6f63-5085-ab33-440412ca6044', 'word_count': 875, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8aa14daa-6f63-5085-ab33-440412ca6044'}, {'abstract': 'After a number of setbacks, the former New Jersey governor and Goldman Sachs executive is planning his next act: a hedge fund built for the Trump era.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/18/business/dealbook/jon-corzine-wall-street-comeback.html', 'snippet': 'After a number of setbacks, the former New Jersey governor and Goldman Sachs executive is planning his next act: a hedge fund built for the Trump era.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jon S. Corzine is a 6-foot-2 bear of a man who has spent decades roaming expansive halls of power. He held the top job at the old Goldman Sachs office tower, a concrete pinnacle of American capitalism. And after that, he had the run of the governor’s mansion in New Jersey — all 18,000 square feet of it.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/21/business/21db-corzine1/21db-corzine1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard