live.html', 'snippet': 'No little bowls. Start with healthy specimens. Avoid loners, erratic swimmers and fish with open sores.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Killing goldfish isn’t inevitable,” says Peter Ponzio, a certified goldfish judge and former chairman of the American Goldfish Association and the Goldfish Society of America. Goldfish will eventually die, of course, like all living things. But despite their delicate, fits-in-a-sandwich-bag body, they don’t have to do so prematurely; a common goldfish can live up to 30 years and reach two feet in length.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '35', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/21/magazine/21tip/21tip-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/21/magazine/21tip/21tip-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/21/magazine/21tip/21tip-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/21/magazine/21tip/21tip-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 491, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/21/magazine/21tip/21tip-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 491}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/21/magazine/21tip/21tip-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 837, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/21/magazine/21tip/21tip-superJumbo.jpg', 'height'