-19T11:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francine Prose', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Prose', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/883bb1d1-9061-58fc-85e6-d38ad03dd7a1', 'word_count': 940, 'uri': 'nyt://article/883bb1d1-9061-58fc-85e6-d38ad03dd7a1'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Garodnick, who represents the East Side of Manhattan, is a father, a runner and an enthusiastic resident of Stuyvesant Town-Peter Cooper Village.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/19/nyregion/sunday-routine-councilman-daniel-garodnick.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Garodnick, who represents the East Side of Manhattan, is a father, a runner and an enthusiastic resident of Stuyvesant Town-Peter Cooper Village.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Daniel R. Garodnick, 44, serves on the New York City Council, representing District 4 in Manhattan — a huge swath of the East Side. Since the presidential election, the activity around Trump Tower in Midtown has created headaches for Councilman Garodnick’s constituents, he said, including snarled traffic and a downturn in business for nearby shops. Mr. Garodnick, a Democrat, lives farther south in the district, in Stuyvesant Town-Peter Cooper Village, where he grew up and where he helped forge a major housing preservation deal in 2015. He is married to Zoe Segal-Reichlin, 38, a senior associate general counsel at Planned Parenthood Federation of America; they have two sons, Asher, 6, and Devin, 3. He is also a runner, and trained for the Brooklyn half marathon this weekend.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/21/nyregion/21ROUTINE2/21