of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37c83725-262a-54c3-8fa9-877e7cd3f112', 'word_count': 775, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37c83725-262a-54c3-8fa9-877e7cd3f112'}, {'abstract': 'What best distinguishes human beings from other animals is our foresight, as scientists are just beginning to recognize.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/19/opinion/sunday/why-the-future-is-always-on-your-mind.html', 'snippet': 'What best distinguishes human beings from other animals is our foresight, as scientists are just beginning to recognize.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We are misnamed. We call ourselves Homo sapiens, the “wise man,” but that’s more of a boast than a description. What makes us wise? What sets us apart from other animals? Various answers have been proposed — language, tools, cooperation, culture, tasting bad to predators — but none is unique to humans.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/21/opinion/sunday/21tierney/21tierney-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 455, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/21/opinion/sunday/21tierney/21tierney-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 455}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/21/opinion/sunday/21tierney/21tierney-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 777, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/21/opinion/sunday/21tierney/21tierney-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1149, 'width': 1514, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/21/opinion/sunday/21tierney/21tierney-thumbStandar