oliferation of nuclear weapons. at 17-nation talks in May 1967.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2017/05/19/1967-u-s-and-russia-stall-on-nonproliferation/', 'snippet': 'The United States and Russia were still in disagreement about how to limit the proliferation of nuclear weapons. at 17-nation talks in May 1967.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GENEVA — The United States and the Soviet Union told the resumed disarmament conference today they are still at odds on a treaty to prevent the further spread of nuclear weapons. Both nations promised, however, to do all they can to introduce a joint draft treaty for universal negotiation and acceptance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1967: U.S. and Russia Stall on Nonproliferation', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cold War Era', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-19T12:55:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a0be21d-4a56-5450-a9ff-87fadfc476d0', 'word_count': 249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a0be21d-4a56-5450-a9ff-87fadfc476d0'}, {'abstract': 'For some New Yorkers with the wherewithal, renting is preferable to buying — even when their monthly payments are in the mid-five figures.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/19/realestate/they-can-afford-to-buy-but-they-would-rather-rent.html', 'snippet': 'For some New Yorkers with the wherewithal, renting is preferable to buying — even when their monthly payments are in the mid-five figures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since moving to New York City 16 years ago, Timothy Brown has lived in seven rentals, a succession of studios and one-bedrooms in Brooklyn, Chelsea, Murray Hill and now Kips Bay, where he has been subletting in a postwar high-rise condo for the last three years.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/21/realestate/21HIGHRENTERSCOV/21HIGHRENTERSCOV-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/21/realestate/21HIGHRENTERSCOV/21HIGHRENTERSCOV-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/21/realestate/21HIGHRENTERSCOV/21HIGHRENTERSCOV-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/21/realestate/21HIGHRENTERSCOV/21HIGHRENTERSCOV-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/21/realestate/21HIGHRENTERSCOV/21HIGHRENTERSCOV-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/21/realestate/21HIGHRENTERSCOV/21HIGHRENTERSCOV-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/21/realestate/21HIGHRENTERSCOV/21HIGHRENTERSCOV-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'They Could Buy, but Why? Meet the High-Renters', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In a City of Renters,  They Can Buy, but Why?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renting and Leasing (Real Estate)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-19T13:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne Kaufman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaufman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f7c0626-c615-5e9e-91b1-e925d4cadace', 'word_count': 1179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f7c0626-c615-5e9e-91b1-e925d4cadace'}, {'abstract': 'Marilyn Stasio’s crime column takes us on a Glasgow bender and into the mind of a Norwegian serial killer. For relief, there’s a trip to rural France.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/19/books/review/the-long-drop-denise-mina-jo-nesbo-the-thirst.html', 'snippet': 'Marilyn Stasio’s crime column takes us on a Glasgow bender and into the mind of a Norwegian serial killer. For relief, there’s a trip to rural France.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s no point waiting for Denise Mina’s two dependable series sleuths, Alex Morrow and Paddy Meehan, to appear in THE LONG DROP (Little, Brown, $26), which is a drastic departure from her brilliant contemporary studies of criminals who prey on Glasgow’s social underclass. This new novel takes its story from the Burnside murders, a true crime spree that horrified the city in the late 1950s. William Watt, the owner of a string of bakery shops, is innocent of the murder of his wife, his sister-in-law and his daughter, but although the police can’t prove otherwise, they’re convinced of his guilt. So Watt sets out to convince them that the real killer is Peter Manuel by — wait for it! — taking him out on a bender and jollying him into a confession.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/21/books/review/0521-BKS-Crime/0521-BKS-Crime-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/21/books/review/0521-BKS-Crime/0521-BKS-Crime-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/21/books/review/0521-BKS-Crime/0521-BKS-Crime-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/21/books/review/0521-BKS-Crime/0521-BKS-Crime-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 730, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/21/books/review/0521-BKS-Crime/0521-BKS-Crime-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 730}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/21/books/review/0521-BKS-Crime/0521-BKS-Crime-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 842, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/21/books/review/0521-BKS-Crime/0521-BKS-Crime-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1684, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'sup