ors at The Times discuss some of their favorite books about how to write well.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If I had to guess, I’d say there are about 85 million books about how to write well. (This week, Jim Holt reviews Harold Evans’s “Do I Make Myself Clear?”) If you tried to read them all you’d never get around to writing, so I asked some of my most bookish colleagues for their favorites in the genre.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/21/books/review/0521-BKS-OpenBook/0521-BKS-OpenBook-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/21/books/review/0521-BKS-OpenBook/0521-BKS-OpenBook-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/21/books/review/0521-BKS-OpenBook/0521-BKS-OpenBook-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/21/books/review/0521-BKS-OpenBook/0521-BKS-OpenBook-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 284, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/21/books/review/0521-BKS-OpenBook/0521-BKS-OpenBook-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 284}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/21/books/review/0521-BKS-OpenBook/0521-BKS-OpenBook-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 484, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/21/books/review/0521-