us/grand-jury-officer-boy-bb-gun-killing.html', 'snippet': 'The fatal encounter in Columbus, Ohio, between a white officer and a black teenager last year quickly polarized the public.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A grand jury in Columbus, Ohio, declined on Friday to indict a white police officer who fatally shot a 13-year-old black boy who was brandishing a BB gun, finding that the officer’s actions were justified, city officials and the police said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Grand Jury Won’t Indict Officer in Killing of Boy, 13, Who Held BB Gun', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Charges for Officer Who Killed Ohio Boy, 13', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Columbus (Ohio)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mason, Bryan (Columbus, Ohio, Police Officer)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Tyre (d 2016)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'BB and Airsoft Guns', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-20T02:25:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Stevens', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stevens', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/104dfc67-6ca1-58e8-869e-28b556c05673', 'word_count': 560, 'uri': 'nyt://article/104dfc67-6ca1-58e8-869e-28b556c05673'}, {'abstract': 'Most historians say no — but not all agree. We should hear them out.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/19/opinion/was-vietnam-winnable.html', 'snippet': 'Most historians say no — but not all agree. We should hear them out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My interest in the Vietnam War began in the early 1990s, when I took a college course on the history of the conflict. Part of what drew me to the subject was the visceral contempt that my peers, professors and intellectuals generally had not just for the war, but for its veterans. It seemed to me a profound wrong that the young men who had risked their lives in Southeast Asia were deemed less worthy than those who had stayed safe at home.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/20/opinion/20moyar1web/20moyr1web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 406, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/20/opinion/20moyar1web/20moyr1web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 406}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/20/opinion/20moyar1web/20moyr1web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/20/opinion/20moyar1web/20moyr1web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1387, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/20/opinion/20moyar1web/20moyar1web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/20/opinion/20moyar1web/20moyar1web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/20/opinion/20moyar1web/20moyar1web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 't