en, Andrea (Journalist)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anxiety and Stress', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-21T21:12:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/42d2b454-0627-54a9-8312-d0ac2067bc52', 'word_count': 839, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42d2b454-0627-54a9-8312-d0ac2067bc52'}, {'abstract': 'Four obsessives at The New York Times and one newbie help you unpack the glories of a deeply American artifact as it stars its first black lead.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/21/arts/television/bachelorette-rachel-lindsay-guide.html', 'snippet': 'Four obsessives at The New York Times and one newbie help you unpack the glories of a deeply American artifact as it stars its first black lead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is a mantra often repeated on “The Bachelor” and its spinoff, “The Bachelorette”: “Here for the right reasons.” Contestants who go on the show to put their trust in “the process,” find true love and settle down are “here for the right reasons.” Those who come to take off their tops, boost their Instagram followings and land hosting gigs on the spring break party circuit are not.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/22/arts/22BACHELORETTE-MAIN-GRID/22BACHELORETTE-MAIN-GRID-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 