 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87de836b-dbb9-575d-ab83-7be890e90940', 'word_count': 83, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87de836b-dbb9-575d-ab83-7be890e90940'}, {'abstract': 'This plastic invention takes some of the pain out of peeling hard-cooked eggs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/22/dining/egg-peeler-gadget-negg.html', 'snippet': 'This plastic invention takes some of the pain out of peeling hard-cooked eggs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This clever plastic egg peeler really works. Place a hard-cooked egg in the container, add a little water, cover and shake up and down until the sound the egg makes diminishes. Then it will be a cinch to peel. Without the Connecticut-made gadget, invented by a home cook with too many deviled eggs to prepare, you could use a jelly jar with some water almost as effectively: The Negg, $17.99, neggmaker.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/24/dining/24BURNER-EGG/24BURNER-EGG-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/24/dining/24BURNER-EGG/24BURNER-EGG-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/24/dining/24BURNER-EGG/24BURNER-EGG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/24/dining/24BURNER-EGG/24BURNER-EGG-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'capti