'}, {'abstract': 'In this reimagined version of Shakespeare’s tragedy, the Prince of Denmark becomes the Prince of Persia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/22/theater/hamlet-review-sheen-center.html', 'snippet': 'In this reimagined version of Shakespeare’s tragedy, the Prince of Denmark becomes the Prince of Persia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As if the poor guy weren’t conflicted enough, Hamlet has taken on an extra burden of ambivalence in the new Waterwell production of the play that bears his name. In addition to worrying about all the usual melancholy Dane stuff — whether to be or not to be, act or not to act, help or hurt his mom — he is now torn (to pieces) between cultural identities.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/23/arts/23HAMLET1/23HAMLET1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/23/arts/23HAMLET1/23HAMLET1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/23/arts/23HAMLET1/23HAMLET1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/23/arts/23HAMLET1/23HAMLET1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1199, 'width': 1799, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/23/arts/23HAMLET1/23HAMLET1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/23/arts/23HAMLET1/23HAMLET1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/23/arts/23HAMLET1/23HAMLET1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A ‘Hamlet’ Poised Between Cultures (and Languages)', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A ‘Hamlet’ Poised Between Two Worlds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Hamlet (Play)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sheen Center', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Waterwell', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moayed, Arian', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ridgely, Tom', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-22T21:06:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/89be162c-8011-5aec-9201-3f7eb2744444', 'word_count': 940, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89be162c-8011-5aec-9201-3f7eb2744444'}, {'abstract': 'The return of the Log Lady and a mysterious glass box are among the Lynchian touches in the first episodes of the new “Twin Peaks.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/22/arts/television/twin-peaks-season-3-episodes-1-2-recap.html', 'snippet': 'The return of the Log Lady and a mysterious glass box are among the Lynchian touches in the first episodes of the new “Twin Peaks.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Part of what made the first season of “Twin Peaks” so popular back in 1990 was that it filtered the director David Lynch’s surrealistic excesses through the more ordered mind of the TV veteran Mark Frost. After all the speculation and worry about what Showtime’s new version of the series would be, this week’s double-length opening salvo ended up balancing the disturbingly strange with the merely quirky and the somewhat normal, resulting — yet again — in something as surprisingly accessible as it is singularly bizarre. Two hours in, the third season is already perplexing, unsettling and potentially addicting.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/22/watching/22twinpeaks/22twinpeaks-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/22/watching/22twinpeaks/22twinpeaks-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/22/watching/22twinpeaks/22twinpeaks-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/22/watching/22twinpeaks/22recaps-slide-AIZT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/22/watching/22twinpeaks/22recaps-slide-AIZT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/22/watching/22twinpeaks/22recaps-slide-AIZT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/22/watching/22twinpeaks/22recaps-slide-AIZT-s