graph': 'If you visit the Vietnam Veterans Memorial, go to Panel 20, Line 3. It is near the top, so you might have to crane your neck. There you will find the name Donald M. Peterson. Pete, as he was known to his buddies, was the lone American to die in a small-scale battle that took place in the Mekong Delta on May 15, 1967 — a battle recounted in a column in this series last week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/23/opinion/23weistWeb/23weistWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 883, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/23/opinion/23weistWeb/23weistWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 883}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/23/opinion/23weistWeb/23weistWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 697, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/23/opinion/23weistWeb/23weistWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1393, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/23/opinion/23weistWeb/23weistWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/23/opinion/23weistWeb/23weistWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/23/opinion/23weistWeb/23weistWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When the War Came Home', 'kicker': "Vie