arge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Bombing at a Manchester Concert', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Bombing at a Manchester Concert', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Manchester Arena Bombing (May, 2017)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manchester (England)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-23T19:24:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/98f7d4b2-d0af-52a7-a935-0c863ceb5679', 'word_count': 373, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98f7d4b2-d0af-52a7-a935-0c863ceb5679'}, {'abstract': 'A rooftop bar from Dale Talde, Empellón Cocina closes, and other restaurant news.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/23/dining/180-tenth-by-smorgasburg-opens-at-the-high-line-hotel.html', 'snippet': 'A rooftop bar from Dale Talde, Empellón Cocina closes, and other restaurant news.', 'lead_paragraph': '180 TENTH BY SMORGASBURG The leafy, welcoming terrace in front of the High Line Hotel is ready for its seasonal run. This year, it will be in the hands of Eric Demby, the organizer and operator of markets and food halls like Smorgasburg, Brooklyn Flea and Berg’n, and his business partner, Jonathan Butler. Instead of curating a collection of vendors, Mr. Demby will be running the restaurant and bar. In the kitchen he has put Aaron Taber, who was at David Chang’s Maple, a food delivery service that is now defunct. The menu is long on smaller items like oysters, arancini, crudités, charcuterie plates and pickles. Salads and vegetables, some served with eggs, and a few more substantial dishes, including burgers, round out the choices. Drinks like Tom Collins and frozen negronis are suitably summery. Mr. Demby said he was “quite excited” at the prospect of opening a real restaurant. Dinner will be followed by brunch on June 10 and weekday lunches starting on June 19. (Opens Thursday): High Line Hotel, 180 10th Avenue (20th Street), 212-933-9735, 180tenth.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/24/dining/24OFF/24OFF-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/24/dining/24OFF/24OFF-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 394}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/24/dining/24OFF/24OFF-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/24/dining/24OFF/24OFF-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1344, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/24/dining/24OFF/24OFF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/24/dining/24OFF/24OFF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/24/dining/24OFF/24OFF-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '180 Tenth by Smorgasburg Opens at the High Line Hotel', 'kicker': 'Off the Menu', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name':