yt://article/8d3cf466-b5b2-5c16-a3ce-6df1cec27b9f'}, {'abstract': 'The comeback of distressed and lost communities is the story of Bill Clinton’s America, not Donald Trump’s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/24/opinion/rusting-and-rising-america.html', 'snippet': 'The comeback of distressed and lost communities is the story of Bill Clinton’s America, not Donald Trump’s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OAK RIDGE, Tenn. — In his dystopian Inaugural Address, President Trump painted a picture of America as a nation gripped by vast “carnage” — a landscape of “rusted-out factories scattered like tombstones” that cried out for a strongman to put “America first” and stop the world from stealing our jobs. It was a shocking speech in many ways and reportedly prompted former President George W. Bush to say to those around him on the dais, “That was some really weird [stuff].”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/24/opinion/24friedman/24friedman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1263, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/24/opinion/24friedman/24friedman-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1263}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/24/opinion/24friedman/24friedman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 487, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/24/opinion/24friedman/24friedman-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 973, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/24/opinion/24friedman/24friedman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'h