iry (or “interrogations,” as academics like to say) concern themselves with power dynamics imposed by cultural norms, including those that conspire to make physicality itself a form of trauma.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/28/books/review/0528-BKS-Egos/0528-BKS-Egos-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1235, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/28/books/review/0528-BKS-Egos/0528-BKS-Egos-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1235}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/28/books/review/0528-BKS-Egos/0528-BKS-Egos-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 498, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/28/books/review/0528-BKS-Egos/0528-BKS-Egos-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 996, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/28/books/review/0528-BKS-Egos/0528-BKS-Egos-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/28/books/review/0528-BKS-Egos/0528-BKS-Egos-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/28/books/review/0528-BKS-Egos/0528-BKS-Egos-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New in Memoir: The Intersex Body, the Dead Body, the Body in Grief', 'kicker': 'Egos', 'content_kicker': None, 