death cell, a choice of a last meal, the final telephone calls and then a lethal injection.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/23/us/24alabama1/24alabama1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/23/us/24alabama1/24alabama1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/23/us/24alabama1/24alabama1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/23/us/24alabama1/24alabama1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/23/us/24alabama1/24alabama1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/23/us/24alabama1/24alabama1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/23/us/24alabama1/24alabama1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Alabama Inmate, 75, Hopes to Dodge Death for an Eighth Time', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After 7 Stays Since 1983, Alabama Inmate Hopes To Stave Off Execution', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arthur, Tommy (1942- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Death Penalty Information Center', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-24T13:43:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Blinder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blinder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9e2f15e-8b24-53f2-8884-cc709a0e0b21', 'word_count': 1288, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9e2f15e-8b24-53f2-8884-cc709a0e0b21'}, {'abstract': 'This group performs at Le Poisson Rouge, with proceeds going to the Equal Justice Initiative.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/24/arts/music/the-jazz-trio-harriet-tubman-in-a-we-resist-concert.html', 'snippet': 'This group performs at Le Poisson Rouge, with proceeds going to the Equal Justice Initiative.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The doom-jazz power trio Harriet Tubman has released four albums over the past 20 years, none thicker with intention and power than its latest, “Araminta.” Recorded in collaboration with the deep-toned trumpeter Wadada Leo Smith, the record wades through an electric mire with a sense of rugged determination, finding a kind of balance but resisting equilibrium. Harriet Tubman — Brandon Ross on guitar, Melvin Gibbs on bass and J.T. Lewis on drums — headlines a concert on Wednesday, May 31, as part of Le Poisson Rouge’s “We Resist” series; proceeds will benefit the Equal Justice Initiative. The show begins at 7 p.m. with a set from the Haitian-born percussionist and turntablist Val-Inc. Also on the bill is the James Brandon Lewis Trio, led by an audacious young tenor saxophonist whose sound is a grimy sluice. That trio is celebrating a release of its own: “No Filter,” its first album, comes out on CD and vinyl on June 9. The guitarist Anthony Pirog joins as a special guest. (212-505-3474, lpr.com.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/28/arts/28GUIDE2/28GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 367, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/28/arts/28GUIDE2/28GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 367}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/28/arts/28GUIDE2/28GUIDE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 626, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/28/arts/28GUIDE2/28GUIDE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1251, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/28/arts/28GUIDE2/28GUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/28/arts/28GUIDE2/28GUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/28/arts/28GUIDE2/28GUIDE2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Jazz Trio Harriet Tubman in a ‘We Resist’ Concert', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pop; Resistance Scored To Doom Jazz', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Le Poisson Rouge', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harriet Tubman (Music Group)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-24T13:49:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Giovanni Russonello', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Giovanni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Russonello', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e08995d1-e846-58ab-bf93-4539bd381377', 'word_count': 169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e08995d1-e846-58ab-bf93-4539bd381377'}, {'abstract': 'The work of pioneering loft-dwelling artists of New York City will be on display in Houston through early August.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/24/arts/design/from-clipper-ships-to-artists-lofts-at-the-menil-collection.html', 'snippet': 'The work of pioneering loft-dwelling artists of New York City will be on display in Houston through early August.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the early 1950s, when Abstract Expressionism was hot and Greenwich Village was the place to be, New York City’s first generation of loft-dwelling artists was forming down near Wall Street and South Street Seaport, in 19th-century buildings that had once produced riggings for clipper ships.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/28/arts/28GUIDE4/28GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/28/arts/28GUIDE4/28GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 667}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/28/arts/28GUIDE4/28GUIDE4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 102