ce39dc014ec'}, {'abstract': '“Radical Bodies,” an exhibition at the New York Public Library for the Performing Arts, looks at works by Ms. Halprin and other pioneers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/24/arts/dance/a-banned-dance-from-anna-halprin-now-celebrated.html', 'snippet': '“Radical Bodies,” an exhibition at the New York Public Library for the Performing Arts, looks at works by Ms. Halprin and other pioneers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York is often cited as the birthplace of postmodern dance, but California deserves credit. “Radical Bodies,” an exhibition at the New York Public Library for the Performing Arts, explores these Golden State roots through the relationship of three pioneering women with strong ties there: Anna Halprin, Simone Forti and Yvonne Rainer. The exhibition covers 1955-1972, when Ms. Halprin formulated her task-based communal works in the Bay Area and shared them with Ms. Forti and Ms. Rainer, who became influential figures in the New York scene in that period. (Through Sept. 16; nypl.org.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/28/arts/28GUIDE3/28GUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/28/arts/28GUIDE3/28GUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/28/arts/28GUIDE3/28GUIDE3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/28/arts/28GUIDE3/28GUIDE3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1638, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/28/arts/28GUIDE3/28GUIDE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/28/arts/28GUIDE3/28GUIDE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/28/arts/28GUIDE3/28GUIDE3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Banned Dance From Anna Halprin, Now Celebrated', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dance; California Pioneers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Forti, Simone', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Halprin, Anna', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rainer, Yvonne', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Radical Bodies (Exhibit)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-24T13:53:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Schaefer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schaefer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/daf101fa-75b8-59a7-99ac-59cec49b0459', 'word_count': 171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/daf101fa-75b8-59a7-99ac-59cec49b0459'}, {'abstract': 'Programs at Carnegie Hall will focus on vocal works. Matthew Polenzani and Susan Graham are among the stars on the calendar.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/24/arts/music/a-mahler-focus-for-the-met-orchestra-and-esa-pekka-salonen.html', 'snippet': 'Programs at Carnegie Hall will focus on vocal works. Matthew Polenzani and Susan Graham are among the stars on the calendar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Esa-Pekka Salonen had an acclaimed run at the Metropolitan Opera a year ago leading Strauss’s “Elektra.” So it was little surprise when he was tapped, in the midst of those performances, to replace James Levine in the Met Orchestra’s traditional post-opera-season outing at Carnegie Hall a year hence. Those concerts have arrived, and the Met forces travel to Carnegie on Wednesday, May 31; June 3; and June 6.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/28/arts/28GUIDE1/28GUIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/28/arts/28GUIDE1/28GUIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/28/arts/28GUIDE1/28GUIDE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 734, 'width': 734, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/28/arts/28GUIDE1/28GUIDE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 734, 'width': 734, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/28/arts/28GUIDE1/28GUIDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/28/arts/28GUIDE1/28GUIDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/28/arts/28GUIDE1/28GUIDE1-thumbLa