r depictions of dystopias.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/24/arts/television/the-handmaids-tale-the-other-side-recap.html', 'snippet': 'This episode feels like a rote collage of imagery culled from countless other depictions of dystopias.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Handmaid’s Tale” is very good at imbuing simple and quiet moments — a trip to the gynecologist, Serena Joy pruning her rose garden, a game of Scrabble — with high suspense. Scenes often include emotional turns and narrative twists that resonate long after the characters stop speaking. Its suspense often leaves me in a state of anxiety. This series may have its blindspots (which I’ve written about several times before), but I have always been riveted by its story and curious about its characters. Until now.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/22/watching/24handmaid/22recaps-slide-ID2I-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/22/watching/24handmaid/22recaps-slide-ID2I-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/22/watching/24handmaid/22recaps-slide-ID2I-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/22/watching/24handmaid/22recaps-slide-ID2I-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/22/watching/24handmaid/22recaps-slide-ID2I-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017