, 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-24T19:27:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e1f8309-44b2-5833-88e4-f7d297776764', 'word_count': 63, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e1f8309-44b2-5833-88e4-f7d297776764'}, {'abstract': 'Now out of bankruptcy, New York City Opera will present “Brokeback Mountain,” which it commissioned nearly a decade ago, in its 2017-18 season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/24/arts/music/city-opera-to-stage-brokeback-mountain-new-season.html', 'snippet': 'Now out of bankruptcy, New York City Opera will present “Brokeback Mountain,” which it commissioned nearly a decade ago, in its 2017-18 season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During his brief, troubled tenure heading New York City Opera a decade ago as it was hurtling toward bankruptcy, the visionary European impresario Gerard Mortier commissioned Charles Wuorinen to write an opera based on “Brokeback Mountain.” But Mr. Mortier left the company almost before he began, and his American opera eventually had its premiere in Madrid.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/25/arts/25cityopera-item/25cityopera-item-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/25/arts/25cityopera-item/25cityopera-item-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/25/arts/25cityopera-item/25cityopera-item-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'cred