318-b676-5ff7-a3fe-1d80af7f26ea'}, {'abstract': 'Flamingos don’t appear to need to flex their muscles to maintain their classic one-legged posture, a new study suggests.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/24/science/flamingos-one-leg-stance-muscle.html', 'snippet': 'Flamingos don’t appear to need to flex their muscles to maintain their classic one-legged posture, a new study suggests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Squat down as if you’re going to sit in a chair. Make sure to keep your back straight, use your hips as a hinge and push your butt backward. Try not to lean forward. Maintain your knees and ankles at 90-degree angles. Now try it on just one leg, and then swap that one with the other. To make it even harder, stand on a foam mat — and close your eyes.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/25/science/24FLAMINGO2/24FLAMINGO2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/25/science/24FLAMINGO2/24FLAMINGO2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 391}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/25/science/24FLAMINGO2/24FLAMINGO2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 668, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/25/science/24FLAMINGO2/24FLAMINGO2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1335, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/25/science/24FLAMINGO2/24FLAMINGO2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail