word_count': 291, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59521731-dd92-580d-93b0-c0745887fd6c'}, {'abstract': 'Teresa Palmer has a breakthrough role as a young woman on holiday in Berlin whose instant romance with a stranger results in her abduction.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/25/movies/berlin-syndrome-review.html', 'snippet': 'Teresa Palmer has a breakthrough role as a young woman on holiday in Berlin whose instant romance with a stranger results in her abduction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Teresa Palmer’s work in the opening minutes of “Berlin Syndrome” succeeds in conveying the nearly tactile sensations of being an enthusiastic stranger in a strange land. Playing Clare, an Australian photographer looking for inspiration and adventure in Berlin, she seems to aspire to walk on air as she emerges from a subway station; a little later, leaning over the railing of the roof of the youth hostel where she’s staying, she looks similarly ready to take off.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/26/arts/26BERLINSYNDROME/26BERLINSYNDROME-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/26/arts/26BERLINSYNDROME/26BERLINSYNDROME-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/26/arts/26BERLINSYNDROME/26BERLINSYNDROME-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/26/arts/26BERLINSYNDROME/26BERLINSYNDROME-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 880, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/