of the playwright’s heroines from “A Midsummer Night’s Dream.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/25/movies/hermia-and-helena-review.html', 'snippet': 'Matías Piñeiro’s follows the trials, tribulations and romances inspired by two of the playwright’s heroines from “A Midsummer Night’s Dream.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Starting with “Rosalinda” in 2010, the Argentine filmmaker Matías Piñeiro has been making what he calls “Shakespeareads,” modern-day stories inspired by the playwright’s heroines. Which is not to say that you need to brush up on your Shakespeare to engage with “Hermia & Helena,” the latest in Mr. Piñeiro’s series and the first one set in the United States.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/26/arts/26HERMIA/26HERMIA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/26/arts/26HERMIA/26HERMIA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/26/arts/26HERMIA/26HERMIA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/26/arts/26HERMIA/26HERMIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 541, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/26/arts/26HERMIA/26HERMIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 541}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/26/arts/26HERMIA/26HERMIA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype':