611-c7b0d26efb67'}, {'abstract': 'Darren Hayman released four albums with the indie band Hefner. Now he writes songs about the communities whose soldiers all returned home safely from World War I.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/25/arts/music/darren-hyman-thankful-villages-songs.html', 'snippet': 'Darren Hayman released four albums with the indie band Hefner. Now he writes songs about the communities whose soldiers all returned home safely from World War I.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SHROPSHIRE, England — One recent Saturday, Darren Hayman drove three and a half hours from London to Harley in Shropshire, a well-to-do village among rolling hills made up of 75 houses and a Norman church with a notice boasting it had just installed carpeting. Mr. Hayman, 46, a cult British songwriter, was there to record a song about the villager Hilda Preece, who in the early 1900s, he said, “held prototype raves in a barn, putting gramophones in, everyone dancing all night.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/26/arts/26HAYMAN1/26HAYMAN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/26/arts/26HAYMAN1/26HAYMAN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/26/arts/26HAYMAN1/26HAYMAN1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/26/arts/26HAYMAN1/26HAYMAN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 362, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/26/arts/26HAYMAN1/26HAYMAN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 362}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/26/arts/26HAYMAN1/26HAYMAN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 619, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/26/arts/26HAYMAN1/26HAYMAN1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1237, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Finding Songs Hidden in Britain’s Thankful Villages', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Village Songster', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Thankful Villages Vol 2 (Album)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hayman, Darren', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-25T22:03:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Marshall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Marshall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d485111f-2845-5818-91b6-5993c8dcdaf3', 'word_count': 701, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d485111f-2845-5818-91b6-5993c8dcdaf3'}, {'abstract': 'Federal prosecutors charged Vitaly Borker, who spent over three years in prison for threatening customers of his previous online business, with wire and mail fraud.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/25/business/eyeglass-vendor-imprisoned-for-terrorizing-consumers-is-accused-of-fraud.html', 'snippet': 'Federal prosecutors charged Vitaly Borker, who spent over three years in prison for threatening customers of his previous online business, with wire and mail fraud.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vitaly Borker served a three-and-a-half-year stint in prison for threatening to stalk, maim and murder customers of his online eyeglass store, DecorMyEyes. But the court-ordered timeout, it seems, did little to convince him to take a new approach to sales.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/26/business/26EYEGLASS/26EYEGLASS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/26/business/26EYEGLASS/26EYEGLASS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/26/business/26EYEGLASS/26EYEGLASS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/26/business/26EYEGLASS/26EYEGLASS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/26/business/26EYEGLASS/26EYEGLASS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/26/business/26EYEGLASS/26EYEGLASS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/26/business/26EYEGLASS/26EYEGLASS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1348, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Eyeglass Vendor, Imprisoned for Terrorizing Consumers, Is Accused of Fraud', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Charges for Purveyor Of Eyeglasses and Threats', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customer Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'DecorMyEyes.com', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'OpticsFast Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Borker, Vitaly', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-25T22:05:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Segal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Segal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20abb6e7-a131-5d91-ad24-09572d80e2a2', 'word_count': 942, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20abb6e7-a131-5d91-ad24-09572d80e2a2'}, {'abstract': 'Proposed cuts in President Trump’s budget to food assistance programs would make the country’s hunger problem even worse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/25/nyregion/trump-budget-austerity-food-pantries.html', 'snippet': 'Proposed cuts in President Trump’s budget to food assistance programs would make the country’s hunger problem even worse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As soon as it was released, President Trump’s budget, titled “A New Foundation for American Greatness,” was characterized by politicians and ordinary human beings of various leanings as the manifesto of someone who seemed to wish he were running a Victorian orphanage. Greatness, in the context of the administration’s economic ideology, is built on a ground laid thick with self-abnegation. It is demanded not on the part of the well off, who are mandated instead to indulge themselves — spending the money they might have otherwise paid in taxes on Jet Skis and lake houses — but from those who are not typically in a position to decide whether it’s wild Alaskan salmon or a grass-fed rib-eye for dinner tonight.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/28/nyregion/28BIG1/28BIG1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/28/nyregion/28BIG1/28BIG1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/28/nyregion/28BIG1/28BIG1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/28/nyregion/28BIG1/28BIG1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/28/nyregion/28BIG1/28BIG1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/28/nyregion/28BIG1/28BIG1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/28/nyregion/28BIG1/28BIG1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Even in Liberal Cities, Budgets Push Austerity Into Starvation Territory', 'kicker': 'Big City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Budgets Are Pushing Austerity Into Starvation Territory', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Banks and Pantries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Stamps', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-25T22:09:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metropolitan', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ginia Bellafante', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ginia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bellafante', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f2c25c2-78c0-5a7a-867a-8125712b4819', 'word_count': 980, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f2c25c2-78c0-5a7a-867a-8125712b4819'}, {'abstract': 'A wealthy candidate overcame a crisis of his own making, winning a closely watched contest a day after he was accused of physically attacking a reporter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/25/us/montana-special-election.html', 'snippet': 'A wealthy candidate overcame a crisis of his own making, winning a closely watched contest a day after he was accused of physically attacking a reporter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOZEMAN, Mont. — Greg Gianforte, a wealthy Montana Republican who was charged with assaulting a reporter on Wednesday, nonetheless won the state’s lone seat in the House of Representatives on Thursday, according to The Associated Press, in a special election held up as a test of the country’s political climate.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1