al guarantors, as shown by the $110.5 million bid for a Jean-Michel Basquiat painting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Occasionally, the art market achieves a truly exceptional price that makes headlines round the world, leaves experts in shock and makes millions of people view an artist in a different way. The $39.9 million paid at Christie’s in 1987 for Van Gogh’s “Sunflowers” was one such result. The $110.5 million bid last week at Sotheby’s for Jean-Michel Basquiat’s 1982 Neo-Expressionist painting of a skull, “Untitled,” may well be another.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/18/arts/18BASQUIAT/18BASQUIAT-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/18/arts/18BASQUIAT/18BASQUIAT-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/18/arts/18BASQUIAT/18BASQUIAT-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/18/arts/18BASQUIAT/18BASQUIAT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 637, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/18/arts/18BASQUIAT/18BASQUIAT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 637}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/18/arts/18BASQUIAT/18BASQUIAT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 965, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/18/arts/18BASQUIAT/18BASQUIAT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2031, 