, 'snippet': 'Under Julie Kent’s direction, the company hits peaks in a program that includes Anthony Tudor’s “Jardin aux Lilas” and Frederick Ashton’s “The Dream.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Julie Kent — the longest-serving ballerina in American Ballet Theater’s history until her retirement in 2015 — is establishing her own style as artistic director of the Washington Ballet. Among other features, she has established the tradition of making an introductory speech before performances. It works: She has charm, a spectacular dress sense and a manner of speaking both fluent and measured. It also gives the welcome impression that she’s proud to take responsibility for what follows.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/27/arts/27washballet/27washballet-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/27/arts/27washballet/27washballet-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/27/arts/27washballet/27washballet-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/27/arts/27washballet/27washballet-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 601, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/27/arts/27washballet/27washballet-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 601}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/27/arts/27washballet/27washballet-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1023, 'subType': 'jumbo', '