to me. Or so I’d thought.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The Fastnet yacht race starts from Cowes, on the Isle of Wight, off the south coast of England. Competitors head west along the English Channel, go around Land’s End, and across the Celtic Sea to the desolate Fastnet Rock off the southern extremity of Ireland. The race returns to make its finish in Plymouth, Devon, in southwest England. The voyage takes most boats about five days and is one of the classics of offshore racing, notorious for rough water and sudden gales.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/26/opinion/27hutchinson1web/27hutchinson1web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/26/opinion/27hutchinson1web/27hutchinson1web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/26/opinion/27hutchinson1web/27hutchinson1web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/26/opinion/27hutchinson1web/27hutchinson1web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/26/opinion/27hutchinson1web/27hutchinson1web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 382}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/26/opinion/27hutchinson1web/27hutchinson1web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 651, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/20