], 'pub_date': '2017-05-27T02:23:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel Lewis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lewis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/9aecc7bd-1f26-562e-8a2f-7ef33ad6b78a', 'word_count': 2049, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9aecc7bd-1f26-562e-8a2f-7ef33ad6b78a'}, {'abstract': 'DeGrom, the ace of an injury-riddled staff, gave up one run in eight and a third innings. Neil Walker powered the offense with two home runs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/26/sports/baseball/new-york-mets-pittsburgh-pirates-jacob-degrom.html', 'snippet': 'DeGrom, the ace of an injury-riddled staff, gave up one run in eight and a third innings. Neil Walker powered the offense with two home runs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PITTSBURGH — With one out in the ninth inning Friday night, Jacob deGrom walked off the mound for good at PNC Park. The sparse crowd of Mets fans behind the visiting team’s dugout stood and applauded.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/27/sports/27mets2/27mets2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/27/sports/27mets2/27mets2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/27/sports/27mets2/27mets2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/27/spor