1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48f0aecb-9cbf-53a4-ac7e-bdbf005d2d2d'}, {'abstract': 'Love isn’t always black and white, and the photographer Andre Wagner shows the range of the emotion through his gray-scale images.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/27/style/brooklyn-photos-love-bed-stuy-bushwick-andre-wagner.html', 'snippet': 'Love isn’t always black and white, and the photographer Andre Wagner shows the range of the emotion through his gray-scale images.', 'lead_paragraph': '“One of the things that I noticed quickly,”  the photographer Andre Wagner said of moving to Bushwick, Brooklyn, from Omaha in 2012, is “how you can see the affection of people out in public because so many things happen on the streets.” Mr. Wagner drew upon his background in social work when he started taking photos. “Living in Brooklyn, I see a lot of that family interaction, which I’m really interested in capturing.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Capturing Love, the Brooklyn Way', 'kicker': 'the look', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-27T10:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andre Wagner, Joanna Nikas and Eve Lyons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andre', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wagner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Joanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nikas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Eve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'ny