e cars are produced here and (b) Germany has a reputation for producing good cars. Why shouldn’t a country export goods in which it has a comparative advantage? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Germany’s Real Sin', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2017-05-27T14:52:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35098085-fe4b-50eb-935f-740a5616294a', 'word_count': 299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35098085-fe4b-50eb-935f-740a5616294a'}, {'abstract': 'Some criticize writing about the fashion statements of public figures like Melania Trump. But sartorial choices tell us a lot about a person.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/27/insider/melania-trump-political-fashion.html', 'snippet': 'Some criticize writing about the fashion statements of public figures like Melania Trump. But sartorial choices tell us a lot about a person.', 'lead_paragraph': 'These days, every time I sit down to write about the clothes worn by a political figure, I have to take a deep breath. I wrote this week about the image engineering of the first lady, Melania Trump, as she accompanied her husband on his first trip abroad, and I know pretty soon the hate tweets are going to start flooding in. “You idiot, why are you writing about what they wear!” “How dare you normalize them!” “Oh, right: Clothes are so much more important than the budget, you airhead.” And so on.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/28/insider/28-a2-insider-COMBO/28-a2-insider-COMBO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/28/insider/28-a2-insider-COMBO/28-a2-insider-COMBO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/28/insider/28-a2-insider-COMBO/28-a2-insider-COMBO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/28/insider/28-a2-insider-COMBO/28-a2-insider-COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/28/insider/28-a2-insider-COMBO/28-a2-insider-COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/28/insider/28-a2-insider-COMBO/28-a2-insider-COMBO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/28/insider/28-a2-insider-COMBO/28-a2-insider-COMBO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How the Clothes Make the First Lady', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Why Wardrobe Choices Matter, From Elizabeth I to Melania Trump', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Melania', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'First Ladies (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-27T15:09:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Insider', 'section_name': 'Times Insider', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vanessa Friedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vanessa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd58252f-b585-5a9a-948f-fea89d3eaa6d', 'word_count': 685, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd58252f-b585-5a9a-948f-fea89d3eaa6d'}, {'abstract': 'Bryan Herta, a former driver and team owner, has become the strategist for Marco Andretti, who will start eighth in the Indianapolis 500.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/27/sports/autoracing/marco-andretti-bryan-herta-indianapolis-500.html', 'snippet': 'Bryan Herta, a former driver and team owner, has become the strategist for Marco Andretti, who will start eighth in the Indianapolis 500.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No other family has as much knowledge about the things that can happen in open-wheel racing, good and bad, as the Andrettis of Nazareth, Pa.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/28/sports/28ANDRETTIweb3/28ANDRETTIweb3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/28/sports/28ANDRETTIweb3/28ANDRETTIweb3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/28/sports/28ANDRETTIweb3/28ANDRETTIweb3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': Non