pe_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4013838-f968-5822-a836-96724b621081', 'word_count': 386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4013838-f968-5822-a836-96724b621081'}, {'abstract': 'As with many of Ms. Copeland’s performances, she was best in low-pressure moments, and more captivating as an actor than a dancer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/28/arts/dance/misty-copelands-down-to-earth-debuts-in-don-quixote-and-giselle.html', 'snippet': 'As with many of Ms. Copeland’s performances, she was best in low-pressure moments, and more captivating as an actor than a dancer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The potential oppressiveness of what many people consider to be ideal is something that Misty Copeland most likely considered before becoming the first African-American female principal dancer at American Ballet Theater two years ago. And it’s probably on her mind now, as she tackles more and more canonical roles, working out how to make them her own. At the Metropolitan Opera on May 16, she debuted as Kitri, the female lead in “Don Quixote,” and on Friday, she performed the title part in “Giselle” in New York for the first time.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/29/arts/29MISTY2/29MISTY2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/29/arts/29MISTY2/29MISTY2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/29/arts/29MISTY2/29MISTY2-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/29/arts/29MISTY2/29MISTY2-articl