ard-and-more.html', 'snippet': 'The best of this spring’s cookbooks remind us of the meaning and value of home-cooked meals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anyone who likes to cook probably walks around the kitchen accompanied by a chorus of instructions gleaned from years of standing stove-side with Grandma or sitting couch-side with Ina. The best cookbooks play a role too — and the measure of a successful one comes down to this: How long does it stay with you? How long do you walk around with the author’s voice in your head? This spring, more than a few pass that test, needling us not only to, say, use more salt, but reminding us about the meaning and value of home-cooked meals.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '38', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/06/04/books/review/0604-BKS-Cooking/0604-BKS-Cooking-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/06/04/books/review/0604-BKS-Cooking/0604-BKS-Cooking-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/06/04/books/review/0604-BKS-Cooking/0604-BKS-Cooking-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/06/04/books/review/0604-BKS-Cooking/0604-BKS-Cooking-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 435, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/06/04/books/review/0604-BKS-Cooking/0604-BKS-Cooking-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 435}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/06/04/books/review/0604-BKS-Cooking/0604-BKS-Cooking-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 743, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/06/04/books/review/0604-BKS-Cooking/0604-BKS-Cooking-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1046, 'width': 1442, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lemon White Pizza, Smothered Pork Chops, Pea Guacamole: 10 Takes on What to Cook This Summer', 'kicker': 'Summer Reading', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cooking', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Samuelsson, Marcus', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-29T09:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenny Rosenstrach', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenstrach', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/873be882-9869-5e1e-97f8-4407ceadaef4', 'word_count': 3675, 'uri': 'nyt://article/873be882-9869-5e1e-97f8-4407ceadaef4'}, {'abstract': 'A selection of books, for practical use and pleasure reading, that will take readers from their own gardens far into the great outdoors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/29/books/review/outdoors-this-land-jack-spencer-and-more.html', 'snippet': 'A selection of books, for practical use and pleasure reading, that will take readers from their own gardens far into the great outdoors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s a good deal of world’s-end whimpering in the air these days. May I suggest that we begin with a bang — even if it’s merely to journey into the great outdoors? “Bang!” went my heart when I opened the photographer Jack Spencer’s powerful THIS LAND: An American Portrait (University of Texas Press, $45). There isn’t a garden in it — only the vestige of one, vines creeping up the side of a boarded-up cottage in Xenia, Ill., a sign of irrepressible life. As is the disheveled shrubbery lodged in a corner of Max Yasgur’s barn. (And if you have to ask, you didn’t join, in person or in spirit, that ancient odyssey to Woodstock.) This is a book that sets our sights high and fortifies our spirits, even if we merely journey into our own backyards.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/06/04/books/review/0604-BKS-Outdoors/0604-BKS-Outdoors-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/06/04/books/review/0604-BKS-Outdoors/0604-BKS-Outdoors-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/06/04/books/review/0604-BKS-Outdoors/0604-BKS-Outdoors-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/06/04/books/review/0604-BKS-Outdoors/0604-BKS-Outdoors-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 783, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/06/04/books/review/0604-BKS-Outdoors/0604-BKS-Outdoors-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 783}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/06/04/books/review/0604-BKS-Outdoors/0604-BKS