 {'abstract': 'The president believed that the networks were peddling lies and biased reporting to undermine America’s efforts in Vietnam.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/30/opinion/lyndon-johnson-vietnam-war.html', 'snippet': 'The president believed that the networks were peddling lies and biased reporting to undermine America’s efforts in Vietnam.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On May 31, 1967, an ABC news anchor, Frank Reynolds, introduced a film report from Vietnam in an unusual way. He told viewers that they were seeing something unprecedented — a war that television was bringing into their living rooms.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/30/opinion/30pachWeb/30pachWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/30/opinion/30pachWeb/30pachWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/30/opinion/30pachWeb/30pachWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/30/opinion/30pachWeb/30pachWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/30/opinion/30pachWeb/30pachWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/30/opinion/30pachWeb/30pachWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/30/opinion/30pachWeb/30pachWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1372, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lyndon Johnson’s Living Room War', 'kicker': "Vietnam '67", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vietnam War', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Lyndon Baines', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vietnam', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-30T07:21:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chester Pach', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chester', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pach', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb491d3b-9997-537d-85b4-fc3c0409078c', 'word_count': 1581, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb491d3b-9997-537d-85b4-fc3c0409078c'}, {'abstract': 'The market keeps going up, defying the predictions of skeptics. Maybe ideology is clouding our ideas about stocks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/30/opinion/trump-wall-street-stock-market.html', 'snippet': 'The market keeps going up, defying the predictions of skeptics. Maybe ideology is clouding our ideas about stocks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a brief stumble, the stock market returned to its upward march last week and hit another high. This optimism has left many people confused, even infuriated. Why isn’t Wall Street being affected by all the crazy news — including rumors of impeachment — coming out of Washington? Where is the Trump Slump?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/30/opinion/30sharmaWeb/30sharmaWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/30/opinion/30sharmaWeb/30sharmaWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/30/opinion/30sharmaWeb/30sharmaWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/30/opinion/30sharmaWeb/30sharmaWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/05/30/opinion/30sharmaWeb/30sharmaWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/30/opinion/30sharmaWeb/30sharmaWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/30/opinion/30sharmaWeb/30sharmaWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why There Is No ‘Trump Slump’ on Wall Street', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Why No Trump Slump on Wall Street?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-30T07:21:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ruchir Sharma', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ruchir', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sharma', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/8599b513-c540-5e11-8fe5-28de1436bcf3', 'word_count': 975, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8599b513-c540-5e11-8fe5-28de1436bcf3'}, {'abstract': 'All his life he’s served his father or father-in-law. But Kushner is ill-served now by an approach that focuses on tight and exclusive blood bonds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/30/opinion/jared-kushner-russia-meeting.html', 'snippet': 'All his life he’s served his father or father-in-law. But Kushner is ill-served now by an approach that focuses on tight and exclusive blood bonds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jared Kushner deserves a bit of sympathy. All his life he’s been serving his father or father-in-law. All his career he’s been thrust into roles he’s not ready for. His background has ill prepared him for national government. Now he is in a realm where his instincts seem to lead him astray and where there’s a chance he will end up in disgrace and possibly under indictment.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/30/opinion/30brooksWeb/30brooksWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/30/opinion/30brooksWeb/30brooksWeb-thumbSt