nings.html', 'snippet': 'J.G. Melon returns to the Upper West Side, E.A.K. Ramen comes to New York, and other restaurant news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHIL & ANNE’S GOOD TIME LOUNGE For several months, Phil Casaceli, who owns Daddy-O, a West Village bar, had his eye on the former Char No. 4 in Brooklyn. But it wasn’t quite right, he felt, for another Daddy-O. Mutual friends suggested he reach out to the celebrity chef Anne Burrell, whom he already knew, and now they’re opening this restaurant. Ms. Burrell said that she was to ready make the move, though she would by no means be abandoning her television career. Inside, a stretch of bar leads to a dining room with tufted leather banquettes. Above the banquettes, there is shiny orange wallpaper patterned with vinyl records and microphones. Ms. Burrell said that all the dishes are the size of appetizers, and range from light (kale Caesar salad, cauliflower steak) to medium (bucatini all’amatriciana, Korean short ribs with pickled vegetables) to heavy (a burger with two patties, an eight-ounce rib-eye). There’s also an intimate skylit rear dining room. (Opens Wednesday): 196 Smith Street (Baltic Street), Cobble Hill, Brooklyn, 929-337-7817, philandannesgoodtimelounge.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/31/dining/31off/31OFF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/05/31/dining/31off/31OFF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/05/31/dining/31off/31OFF-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'ty