'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/5564e4e5-6385-5763-b8fe-220c965c6e28', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/5564e4e5-6385-5763-b8fe-220c965c6e28'}, {'abstract': 'A branch of Tim Ho Wan and a chef from Din Tai Fung set up in Manhattan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/30/dining/tim-ho-wan-review-pinch-chinese-restaurant-dim-sum-dumpling.html', 'snippet': 'A branch of Tim Ho Wan and a chef from Din Tai Fung set up in Manhattan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Visitors to Hong Kong who have an appreciation for dumplings, an eye toward low prices and faith that a single Michelin star reliably predicts quality will tend to eat at one of two places. Those who are more attracted to Cantonese dim sum classics will almost certainly end up at a location of the locally based Tim Ho Wan chain. The ones whose idea of a perfect dumpling is a xiao long bao with hot broth sealed inside will head to a branch of Din Tai Fung, which was founded in Taiwan. The very hungry ones will go to both.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Dumplings to Hunt, by Way of Hong Kong', 'kicker': 'Restaurant Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Dumpling Hunters, New Ground to Cover', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chinese Food (Cuisine)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Village (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'SoHo (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pinch Chinese (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tim Ho Wan (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-30T19:03:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk