 arrived as part of a slew of female pop rebels who emerged in the wake of Lorde’s early-2010s recalibration of the genre’s operating hierarchies. As had been clear many times before — but was forgotten in the early part of the 2000s — the reluctant girl in the corner or the punk rebel was just as capable of making world-shaping pop as the popular extrovert. Halsey, with her dyed pixie haircut and wild-child interviews, appeared to fit the bill.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/06/01/arts/01HALSEY1/01HALSEY1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/06/01/arts/01HALSEY1/01HALSEY1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/06/01/arts/01HALSEY1/01HALSEY1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/06/01/arts/01HALSEY1/01HALSEY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 406, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/06/01/arts/01HALSEY1/01HALSEY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 406}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/06/01/arts/01HALSEY1/01HALSEY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/06/01/arts/01HALSEY1/01HALSEY1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1386, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Halsey’s Second Album: Something New, but a Lot Borrowed', 'kicker': 'Album Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Something New, but a Lot Borrowed, Too', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Frangipane, Ashley Nicolette (Halsey)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pop and Rock Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'hopeless fountain kingdom (Album)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-31T20:45:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6012ae3-f609-5b59-8386-5439e6e92684', 'word_count': 593, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6012ae3-f609-5b59-8386-5439e6e92684'}, {'abstract': 'Mrs. Sliwa became the bookkeeper, administrator and publicist for the red-beret-wearing neighborhood patrol group her son, Curtis, formed in New York in 1979.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/31/nyregion/francis-sliwa-dead-guardian-angels-supporter.html', 'snippet': 'Mrs. Sliwa became the bookkeeper, administrator and publicist for the red-beret-wearing neighborhood patrol group her son, Curtis, formed in New York in 1979.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Frances Sliwa, who helped her blustery son, Curtis, run the Guardian Angels neighborhood patrol group from a kitchen table in the Canarsie neighborhood of Brooklyn, died on May 23 in that borough. She was 93.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/06/01/nyregion/31SLIWAobit-1-web/31