sister, Lady Utterword. The bohemians have souls, the aristocrats power, and neither knows what to do with them.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/06/01/arts/01HEARTBREAKJP/01HEARTBREAKJP-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/06/01/arts/01HEARTBREAKJP/01HEARTBREAKJP-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/06/01/arts/01HEARTBREAKJP/01HEARTBREAKJP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/06/01/arts/01HEARTBREAKJP/01HEARTBREAKJP-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/06/01/arts/01HEARTBREAKJP/01HEARTBREAKJP-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/06/01/arts/01HEARTBREAKJP/01HEARTBREAKJP-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/06/01/arts/01HEARTBREAKJP/01HEARTBREAKJP-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Shaw’s ‘Heartbreak House’ Gets an Unexpected Visitor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gee, He Looks Familiar', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Heartbreak House (Play)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hartford Stage Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tresnjak, Darko', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shaw, George Bernard', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-05-31T21:26:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jesse Green', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Green', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd670243-9783-58b6-9766-ff83df710867', 'word_count': 1028, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd670243-9783-58b6-9766-ff83df710867'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Udofia mined her family background for what she sees as a true portrait of immigrant experiences in her ongoing theater cycle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/31/theater/mfoniso-udofia-sojourners-her-portmanteau-ufot-cycle.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Udofia mined her family background for what she sees as a true portrait of immigrant experiences in her ongoing theater cycle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After moving to New York City nearly a decade ago, Mfoniso Udofia began to ask herself some hard questions: “Who am I?” and “What does it mean to be both African and American?” She was a recent graduate of the master’s program at American Conservatory Theater in San Francisco, but the four to five auditions a week she was going to weren’t resulting in work. As the daughter of Nigerian immigrants, she found it puzzling to be repeatedly told that she wasn’t “African enough.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/06/04/arts/04UDOFIA1/04UDOFIA1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/06/04/arts/04UDOFIA1/04UDOFIA1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/06/04/arts/04UDOFIA1/04UDOFIA1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/06/04/arts/04UDOFIA1/04UDOFIA1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 933, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/06/04/arts/04UDOFIA1/04UDOFIA1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 933}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/06/04/arts/04UDOFIA1/04UDOFIA1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 659, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/06/04/arts/04UDOFIA1/04UDOFIA1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1317, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nine Plays, One Truth: Mfoniso Udofia on Her Immigrant Experience, and Ours', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nine Plays, One Truth: We Share a Beginning', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Udofia, Mfoniso', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Sojourners (Play)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Her Portmanteau (Play)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 5